const ACC_NAMES={"aleabitoreddit": "Serenity", "SemiAnalysis_": "SemiAnalysis", "Omercheema": "Omer Cheema", "OrnnExchange": "Ornn", "HedgeyeTech": "Felix Wang, CFA", "RYANHINGSHING": "Ryan Leung 梁浩盛, CFA", "FredaDuan": "Freda Duan", "TMTLongShort": "Just Another Pod Guy"};
const DIGEST_BY_RANGE={"1": {"intro": "今日材料聚焦两条线索：高通车用半导体的规模跃升，以及AI智能成本快速下降对算力与收入关系的潜在扰动。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 认为高通将在 2027 年成为最大车用半导体公司。九月季度高通车用收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元，并已超越 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美。这是该机构给出的判断，并非既成事实。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116"]}, {"text": "对比历史，2016 年 10 月高通拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时，NXP 车用业务规模是高通的 8.6 倍；上个季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。即便没有这桩收购，高通也先后超过 ADI（2024 年二季度）、安森美（2025 年一季度）、瑞萨（2025 年四季度）、意法半导体（2026 年一季度），以及德州仪器（2026 年三季度，按该机构估算）。", "refs": ["2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入从 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。执行层面，2024 财年指引 15 亿美元、实际 29 亿；2026 财年指引 35 亿、实际 60 亿，并以 80 亿美元年化收入收官，比原定 2031 财年目标提前五年。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337159041695804"]}, {"text": "路径上，高通绕开电源芯片、微控制器、模拟和传感器的正面竞争，切入数字座舱、ADAS 和连接，并通过收购 Arriver（2022 年）和 Autotalks（2025 年）补齐软硬件平台。上季度该计算与连接业务同比增长 89%，英飞凌和 NXP 只增长 10%–13%。设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增至 2026 年 6 月的 650 亿美元。", "refs": ["2124337163357610272", "2124337161105195142"]}, {"text": "能否在 2027 年登顶取决于季度数据和汇率：按 1.15 欧元/美元，英飞凌 2027 财年车用业务约 103 亿美元；若高通保持 12% 季度环比增长，将在 2027 年三季度于季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0 亿 vs 26.8 亿美元），2027 日历年以 107 亿 vs 105 亿美元胜出；若要在 2027 财年胜出，12 月之后需 17.5% 的季度增速。另需注意，@FredaDuan 提出智能成本每季度下降约 47%，代币消耗、模型收入与半导体需求并非同一笔交易。", "refs": ["2124337165437960410", "2124325047120900224"]}], "date": "今天", "note": "短评由编辑基于当日抓取内容撰写，每段后标注来源；文中数字均由脚本回查原文核对。本看板仅做信息整理，不构成投资建议。"}, "3": {"intro": "过去三日，AI交易波动加剧，半导体与算力链多空信息交织，车用半导体竞争格局出现新数据。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达（$NVDA）下跌超过12%，起因是一份新报告称SEC正在调查其潜在的会计问题。有市场参与者指出，连带损伤已开始冲击主要指数和退休投资组合，并提及一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上。上述为市场传闻与个人观察，事实层面尚待公司或监管方确认。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308"]}, {"text": "SemiAnalysis认为高通将在2027年成为最大的车用半导体公司。九月季度高通车用收入首次接近20亿美元（年化约80亿美元），逼近英飞凌的24.5亿美元和NXP的20.7亿美元，并已超越TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI和安森美。其增长与整车销量脱钩，单车车用收入预计从2022年约21美元升至2026年76美元。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337156546080779"]}, {"text": "高通车用设计中标管线从2018年初的30亿美元增长22倍，到2026年6月达650亿美元，是Mobileye 245亿美元管线的2.6倍以上。上季度其计算与连接业务同比增长89%，而英飞凌和NXP仅增长10%–13%。SemiAnalysis测算，若明年保持12%的季度环比增长，高通将在2027年三季度在季度收入上超过英飞凌。", "refs": ["2124337161105195142", "2124337163357610272", "2124337165437960410"]}, {"text": "AI算力链方面，HedgeyeTech称AI交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌5%，并称台湾是最后一个破裂的AI泡沫，其在存储板块持有空头仓位。FredaDuan则引用Epoch AI数据指出，自2023年以来实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%，代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件不同的事，市场往往将其视为同一笔交易。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123731560537149580", "2124325047120900224"]}], "date": "最近 3 天", "note": "短评由编辑基于当日抓取内容撰写，每段后标注来源；文中数字均由脚本回查原文核对。本看板仅做信息整理，不构成投资建议。"}, "7": {"intro": "过去一周，AI交易的情绪面与基本面信号出现明显分化：英伟达遭遇监管传闻冲击，而高通车用半导体的结构性追赶提供了另一条叙事线。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达因一份新报告称SEC正在调查其潜在会计问题而下跌超过12%，连带损伤已冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。同一观察者指出，一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上，令人错愕。另有跟踪半导体的账户称，在其覆盖范围内只有NVDA交易价格接近52周低点，许多低质量公司仍高出2倍甚至4倍。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2123076524861432038"]}, {"text": "AI交易的回撤在区域市场同步显现：韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌5%。有机构称台湾是最后一个破裂的AI泡沫，并披露在存储板块持有空头仓位。与此同时，数据中心相关IPO DayOne被搁置。这些事实共同指向风险偏好收缩，但各账户对持续性判断分歧明显。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123731560537149580", "2123725033272951075"]}, {"text": "高通车用业务在九月季度收入首次接近20亿美元（年化约80亿美元），逼近英飞凌的24.5亿美元和NXP的20.7亿美元，并已超越TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI和安森美。2016年10月高通试图以470亿美元收购NXP时，NXP车用规模是高通的8.6倍，上季度该比值已降至1.04倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自2023年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入从2022到2026年预计增长3.7倍（约从21美元升至76美元）。设计中标管线从2018年初的30亿美元增长22倍，到2026年6月达650亿美元，是Mobileye 245亿美元管线的2.6倍以上。上季度计算与连接业务同比增长89%，英飞凌和NXP仅增长10%–13%。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142", "2124337163357610272"]}, {"text": "能否在2027年超越英飞凌取决于季度数据和汇率。该分析给出的路径是：若明年保持12%的季度环比增长，高通将在2027年一季度超过NXP，三季度在季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0亿 vs 26.8亿美元），并在2027日历年胜出（107亿 vs 105亿美元）；若要在2027财年就胜出，12月之后需要17.5%的季度增速。", "refs": ["2124337165437960410"]}], "date": "最近 7 天", "note": "短评由编辑基于当日抓取内容撰写，每段后标注来源；文中数字均由脚本回查原文核对。本看板仅做信息整理，不构成投资建议。"}, "all": {"intro": "11月18日至22日，AI硬件链出现多重信号：英伟达受会计调查传闻冲击、卖方与买方对Anthropic IPO分歧明显、高通车用半导体逼近英飞凌，同时PCB短缺与算力通缩争论并行。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达单日下跌超过12%，起因是一份新报告称SEC正在调查其潜在会计问题；发帖者称，一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上，连带损伤已冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。同期AI交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌5%。上述为市场表现与传闻层面的事实，调查本身尚无材料内结论。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2123607705969401895"]}, {"text": "Anthropic IPO方面，HedgeyeTech称卖方对其只有买入评级，而其与投资者交流的统计显示58%看空或中性、42%看多。该机构另称2026年7月根据调研判断Anthropic增长动能已见顶、OpenAI复苏，并平掉微软空头；其还称台湾是最后一个破裂的AI泡沫，在存储板块持有空头仓位。", "refs": ["2123625335547998476", "2123035493226975431", "2123731560537149580"]}, {"text": "SemiAnalysis认为高通将在2027年成为最大车用半导体公司：九月季度车用收入首次接近20亿美元（年化约80亿美元），逼近英飞凌的24.5亿美元和NXP的20.7亿美元；单车车用收入预计从2022年约21美元升至2026年约76美元，增长3.7倍。其测算若明年保持12%季度环比增长，高通将在2027年三季度季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0亿 vs 26.8亿美元）。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337156546080779", "2124337165437960410"]}, {"text": "供给端，全球电子协会就PCB供应链日益加剧的短缺发布行业警报，汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信企业报告交期延长，协会称2028年中期前不太可能有实质性缓解。需求端，FredaDuan引用Epoch AI估计，自2023年以来实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%，并指出代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件不同的事。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470", "2124325047120900224"]}], "date": "全部", "note": "短评由编辑基于当日抓取内容撰写，每段后标注来源；文中数字均由脚本回查原文核对。本看板仅做信息整理，不构成投资建议。"}};
const SUMMARIES={"宏观|3": {"intro": "全球电子协会就PCB供应链短缺发布行业警报，AI吸收稀缺产能正波及汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信等行业。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "全球电子协会就印刷电路板（PCB）供应链日益加剧的短缺发布行业警报，汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信行业的公司报告称，随着AI吸收稀缺产能，交货时间延长且难以确保供应，实际上使生产面临风险。该协会表示，在2028年中期之前不太可能有实质性的缓解，并敦促买家提前规划供应限制和制造商。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470"]}, {"text": "超大规模企业已提前规划，如$AMZN入股Gold Circuit Electronics（2368）以确保供应采购。但其他行业的采购未必如此，医疗行业可能不习惯与超大规模企业在同一供应上竞争。由此产生的关键材料短缺，包括CCL和玻璃纤维布，正在挤压消费电子产品的供应。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470"]}, {"text": "市场层面，@HedgeyeTech指出AI交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌5%，并认为随着2027年科技行业前景日益不确定，“便宜”的估值可能因盈利预期被下调而变得更便宜。@aleabitoreddit则感觉所有成长型股票，即便不属于AI领域，从$HOOD到$NBIS，都像是跌下了悬崖。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123732732505444862", "2123805601411277149"]}], "count": 8, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "宏观|7": {"intro": "AI产能挤压正向非AI行业扩散，市场风险偏好明显收缩。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "全球电子协会就PCB供应链日益加剧的短缺发布行业警报，汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信行业公司报告交货时间延长且难以确保供应。该协会表示2028年中期前不太可能有实质缓解，并敦促买家提前规划。@aleabitoreddit 指出，关键材料短缺包括CCL和玻璃纤维布，正挤压消费电子产品供应。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470"]}, {"text": "市场层面，@HedgeyeTech 称AI交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌5%。@aleabitoreddit 观察到所有成长型股票即便不属于AI领域，从$HOOD到$NBIS都像跌下悬崖，而消费必需品领域估值达到自1999年以来未见的高度。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123805601411277149"]}], "count": 15, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "宏观|all": {"intro": "从地缘战略到供应链瓶颈，再到市场风格切换，材料呈现了宏观与产业交织下的多重不确定性。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "推文作者@TMTLongShort称，特朗普的目标并非贸易平衡，而是迫使盟友完全停止与中国的贸易（零进口），以此主动放慢中国工业崛起。该观点认为，此举风险包括中国抛售债券和股票、欧洲缺乏筹码、以及台海局势可能冲击晶圆厂供应。若成功，则可能重塑美国唯一站立的霸权地位。作者强调这不是其倡导，而是掌权者所相信的。", "refs": ["1909491586641047713"]}, {"text": "全球电子协会就PCB供应链短缺发布行业警报，称汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信公司报告交货时间延长且难以确保供应，生产面临风险。该协会表示2028年中期之前不太可能有实质性缓解，并敦促买家提前规划。@aleabitoreddit指出，AI吸收稀缺产能导致CCL和玻璃纤维布等关键材料短缺，挤压消费电子供应，已成为全行业分配问题。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470", "2123859267560304947"]}, {"text": "市场层面，@HedgeyeTech称AI交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌5%，并认为2027年科技行业前景日益不确定，“便宜”估值可能因盈利预期下调而变得更便宜。@aleabitoreddit则观察到，从$HOOD到$NBIS等成长型股票均大幅下跌，而消费必需品领域估值达到自1999年以来未见的高度。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123732732505444862", "2123805601411277149"]}], "count": 16, "range": "全部"}, "行业|1": {"intro": "高通车用半导体收入快速逼近传统龙头，增长主要由单车价值量提升与设计中标管线驱动，但2027年能否登顶仍取决于增速与汇率。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis指出，九月季度高通车用业务收入首次接近20亿美元（年化约80亿美元），逼近英飞凌的24.5亿美元和NXP的20.7亿美元，并已超越TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI和安森美。相比2016年10月拟以470亿美元收购NXP时NXP车用规模为高通的8.6倍，上季度该比值已降至1.04倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "据SemiAnalysis，自2023年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入2022至2026年预计增长3.7倍（约从21美元升至76美元），增长与整车销量脱钩。其设计中标管线从2018年初的30亿美元增长22倍，到2026年6月达650亿美元，为Mobileye 245亿美元管线的2.6倍以上。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142"]}, {"text": "SemiAnalysis称，高通上季度计算与连接业务同比增长89%，英飞凌和NXP仅增长10%–13%。其测算，若明年保持12%的季度环比增长，高通将在2027年三季度以28.0亿对26.8亿美元在季度收入上超过英飞凌，并在2027日历年以107亿对105亿美元胜出；若要在2027财年胜出，12月之后需17.5%的季度增速。", "refs": ["2124337163357610272", "2124337165437960410"]}], "count": 8, "range": "今天"}, "行业|3": {"intro": "高通车用半导体收入快速逼近传统龙头，而AI算力链的供需与成本信号出现分化。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis指出，高通车用业务在九月季度收入首次接近20亿美元（年化约80亿美元），逼近英飞凌的24.5亿美元和NXP的20.7亿美元，并已超越TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI和安森美。与2016年10月试图收购NXP时NXP车用规模是高通8.6倍相比，上季度该比值已降至1.04倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "高通车用增长与整车销量脱钩：自2023年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但单车车用收入从2022到2026年预计增长3.7倍（约从21美元升到76美元）。其设计中标管线从2018年初的30亿美元增长22倍，到2026年6月达650亿美元，是Mobileye 245亿美元管线的2.6倍以上。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142"]}, {"text": "在AI算力侧，FredaDuan引用Epoch AI估计，自2023年以来实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%；OpenRouter在10月处理的代币量几乎是1月的25倍，而同期有效代币价格下降了57-70%。她强调，代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件截然不同的事情，市场往往将它们视为同一笔交易。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}], "count": 21, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "行业|7": {"intro": "本周材料聚焦高通车用半导体的追赶路径与AI算力供需的两种叙事。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 认为高通将在 2027 年成为最大车用半导体公司。九月季度其车用收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元，并已超越 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美。2016 年 10 月高通拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时，NXP 车用规模是高通的 8.6 倍，上个季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入从 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。其设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增长 22 倍，到 2026 年 6 月达 650 亿美元，是 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上。上季度计算与连接业务同比增长 89%，英飞凌和 NXP 只增长 10%–13%。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142", "2124337163357610272"]}, {"text": "对 AI 算力，FredaDuan 引述 Epoch AI 估计，自 2023 年以来实现固定水平 AI 能力的成本每季度下降约 47%，因此其他条件不变时，对智能的消耗需每季度增长约 90% 才能保持相关收入持平。OpenRouter 在 10 月处理的代币量几乎是 1 月的 25 倍，同期有效代币价格下降 57-70%。她强调代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件不同的事。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}], "count": 29, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "行业|all": {"intro": "车用半导体格局位移、AI资本开支节奏与算力通缩三条线索，构成本期行业观察的主轴。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 认为高通有望在 2027 年成为最大车用半导体公司。九月季度其车用收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元；相较 2016 年 10 月高通拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时 NXP 车用规模是高通的 8.6 倍，上季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。其设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增至 2026 年 6 月的 650 亿美元，为 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上；上季度计算与连接业务同比增长 89%，英飞凌和 NXP 只增长 10%–13%。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142", "2124337163357610272"]}, {"text": "资本开支侧存在分歧。FredaDuan 引述腾讯 Martin Lau 的观点称，AI 资本开支将在 2026-27 年见顶、此后强度明显回落；FredaDuan 另引 Epoch AI 估计，自 2023 年以来实现固定水平 AI 能力的成本每季度下降约 47%，并称 OpenRouter 10 月处理代币量几乎是 1 月的 25 倍，同期有效代币价格下降 57-70%。", "refs": ["2123088477868736729", "2124325047120900224"]}], "count": 36, "range": "全部"}, "公司|3": {"intro": "近三日市场围绕AI龙头与IPO的讨论升温，分歧集中于估值、流动性与算力需求。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达（$NVDA）因SEC潜在会计问题调查的报道下跌超12%，@aleabitoreddit称一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上，连带损伤已冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。同日，@RYANHINGSHING提出Ant上市或抽走流动性、波动率上升令半导体股大跌的猜测，但完整内容需订阅。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2123787556626321770"]}, {"text": "围绕Anthropic（$ANT），@HedgeyeTech称卖方只有买入评级，但其与投资者交流统计显示58%看空或中性、42%看多；该机构还称2026年7月调研显示Anthropic增长动能已见顶。@OrnnExchange则追问其8,950亿美元算力支出如何收回，并引述Dario Amodei在CNBC上的看法。", "refs": ["2123625335547998476", "2123035493226975431", "2123811370357690494"]}, {"text": "算力供需信号矛盾：@aleabitoreddit引述$CRWV财报称到2027年全年量化需求是算力可用性的10倍，但同周有人主张算力过剩；该用户还称成长股普跌而消费必需品估值达1999年以来高位。@SemiAnalysis_则转述一则关于黄仁勋与员工GTA 6进度的轶事，并称来源为室友。", "refs": ["2124318494879780986", "2123805601411277149", "2124267194267652470"]}], "count": 10, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "公司|7": {"intro": "近一周市场聚焦英伟达会计调查传闻、Anthropic IPO 预期与 AI 资本开支拐点信号。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达股价单日下跌超过 12%，起因是一份新报告称 SEC 正在调查其潜在会计问题。@aleabitoreddit 指出，一家市值 5 万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌 46% 以上，连带损伤已开始冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。另据 @Omercheema 观察，其跟踪的半导体公司中只有 NVDA 交易价格接近 52 周低点。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2123076524861432038"]}, {"text": "围绕 Anthropic，@HedgeyeTech 称卖方对 $ANT 只有买入评级，但其与投资者交流统计显示 58% 看空或中性、42% 看多；该机构还称 2026 年 7 月调研显示 Anthropic 增长动能已见顶。@OrnnExchange 则援引 Dario Amodei 在 CNBC 上的看法，讨论 8,950 亿美元算力支出如何收回。", "refs": ["2123625335547998476", "2123035493226975431", "2123811370357690494"]}, {"text": "AI 资本开支周期出现分歧信号。@FredaDuan 引述腾讯 Martin Lau 观点：AI 资本开支将在 2026-27 年见顶，2027 年后放缓，理由包括前置投资、2028 年硬件成本下降及效率提升。@aleabitoreddit 则提到 $CRWV 称到 2027 年全年量化需求是算力可用性的 10 倍，与算力过剩论调形成对照。", "refs": ["2123088477868736729", "2124318494879780986"]}], "count": 12, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "公司|all": {"intro": "英伟达会计调查传闻引发股价大跌，AI资本开支节奏与市场情绪同步承压。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达因SEC潜在会计问题调查传闻单日下跌超12%，有推文称其几周内跌幅超46%，并拖累主要指数与退休组合。同期，HedgeyeTech统计投资者对Anthropic IPO看法：58%看空或中性，42%看多，卖方则清一色买入评级。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2123625335547998476"]}, {"text": "资本开支预期出现分歧。FredaDuan引述腾讯总裁刘炽平观点，认为AI资本开支将在2026-27年见顶，理由包括前置投资、硬件成本下降与效率提升。但aleabitoreddit指出，CoreWeave称到2027年量化需求是算力可用性的10倍，与算力过剩论调形成反差。", "refs": ["2123088477868736729", "2124318494879780986"]}, {"text": "市场情绪明显分化。aleabitoreddit称成长股普跌，消费必需品估值达1999年以来高位；Omercheema指出仅NVDA接近52周低点，AMS、AEHR等仍高出2至4倍。此外，DayOne数据中心相关IPO被搁置。", "refs": ["2123805601411277149", "2123076524861432038", "2123725033272951075"]}], "count": 17, "range": "全部"}, "@FredaDuan|1": {"intro": "智能成本快速通缩之下，代币消耗、模型收入与半导体需求并非同一笔交易。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "Epoch AI估计，自2023年以来，实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%；关于模型能力密度的研究则表明，大约每3.5个月就可以用大约一半的参数提供可比性能。@FredaDuan据此指出，曾经需要前沿规模模型才能实现的能力，正越来越多地出现在小得多、便宜得多的模型中。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}, {"text": "这一通缩对增长构成日益苛刻的门槛：在固定水平智能成本每季度下降47%的情况下，其他条件不变时，对这种智能的消耗需要每季度增长约90%，才能仅保持相关收入持平。@FredaDuan援引数据称，OpenRouter在10月处理的代币量几乎是1月的25倍，而同期有效代币价格下降了57-70%。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}, {"text": "但@FredaDuan强调，代币的指数级增长并不会自动转化为收入的指数级增长，更不用说半导体资本支出的持续增长；代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件截然不同的事情，市场却往往将它们视为同一笔交易。过去几年三者相互强化，但不能保证这三条曲线会继续一起移动。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}], "count": 1, "range": "今天"}, "@FredaDuan|3": {"intro": "智能成本快速通缩之下，代币消耗、模型收入与半导体需求并非同一笔交易。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "@FredaDuan 引用 Epoch AI 的估计指出，自2023年以来，实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%；关于模型能力密度的研究则显示，大约每3.5个月就可以用大约一半的参数提供可比性能。作者据此认为，曾经需要前沿规模模型才能实现的能力，正越来越多地出现在更小、更便宜的模型中。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}, {"text": "作者给出一个量化门槛：在固定水平智能成本每季度下降47%的情况下，其他条件不变时，对这种智能的消耗需要每季度增长约90%，才能仅保持相关收入持平。需求侧，OpenRouter在10月处理的代币量几乎是1月的25倍，而同期有效代币价格下降了57-70%。但作者强调，代币的指数级增长不会自动转化为收入的指数级增长。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}, {"text": "作者提醒，过去几年前沿AI进步、代币消耗爆炸式增长与基础设施投资加速在很大程度上相互强化，但不能保证这三条曲线会继续一起移动。其核心判断是：代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件截然不同的事情，而市场往往将它们视为同一笔交易。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}], "count": 1, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@FredaDuan|7": {"intro": "腾讯高管给出AI资本开支2027年后放缓的明确理由，而智能成本快速下降正对需求增长提出更高门槛。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "Martin Lau给出AI资本开支应在2027年后放缓的明确理由：一是前置投资，AI基础设施建成后可持续训练新模型、产出token；二是硬件成本下降，到2028年同样设备成本应低得多；三是效率快速提升，同样基础设施随时间可输出指数级更多训练算力和token。结论是AI资本开支将在2026-27年见顶，此后资本开支强度明显回落，即使AI需求仍在增长。", "refs": ["2123088477868736729"]}, {"text": "Epoch AI估计，自2023年以来实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%；模型能力密度研究显示约每3.5个月可用约一半参数提供可比性能。在固定水平智能成本每季度下降47%下，其他条件不变时，对这种智能的消耗需每季度增长约90%才能仅保持相关收入持平。OpenRouter在10月处理的代币量几乎是1月的25倍，同期有效代币价格下降57-70%。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}], "count": 2, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@FredaDuan|all": {"intro": "从AI资本开支周期到智能成本通缩，再到机器人领域的“GPT-3时刻”，材料呈现了AI产业链不同环节的节奏分化。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "腾讯总裁Martin Lau给出AI资本开支应在2027年后放缓的三点理由：前置投资一旦建成可持续训练新模型、产出token；到2028年同样设备成本应低得多；效率提升使同等基础设施输出指数级更多算力。FredaDuan据此认为，Martin实际上是在说AI资本开支将在2026-27年见顶，此后资本开支强度明显回落，即使AI需求仍在增长。", "refs": ["2123088477868736729"]}, {"text": "FredaDuan引用Epoch AI估计，自2023年以来实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%；模型能力密度研究显示约每3.5个月可用约一半参数提供可比性能。她测算，在成本每季度降47%下，其他条件不变时智能消耗需每季度增长约90%才能保持相关收入持平。OpenRouter在10月处理的代币量几乎是1月的25倍，同期有效代币价格下降57-70%。", "refs": ["2124325047120900224"]}, {"text": "FredaDuan在与50位机器人前沿领域朋友交谈后提出，Astra是机器人领域的GPT-3时刻，并称有消息显示OpenAI围绕核心Astra模型重组了其30至40人的机器人团队，@Tesla_Optimus也有类似转向通用模型的举动。她还提到机器人数据采购达百万小时级、有些可能达数千万小时，有传言称每个前沿实验室的预算接近10亿美元。", "refs": ["2114772074438988256"]}], "count": 8, "range": "全部"}, "@HedgeyeTech|3": {"intro": "HedgeyeTech 在最近 3 天内围绕 $ANT IPO、AI 交易回撤与科技板块估值风险给出了一系列观察。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "HedgeyeTech 指出，卖方对 $ANT 只有买入评级，但其与投资者交流的统计显示，58% 的人看空或中性，42% 看多。该机构还称，2026 年 6 月曾就 $ANT 与 OpenAI 之间的蒸馏漏洞和全球价格战向客户发出警告，2026 年 7 月根据调研判断 Anthropic 增长动能已见顶、OpenAI 复苏，并平掉微软空头。", "refs": ["2123625335547998476", "2123035493226975431"]}, {"text": "在 AI 交易层面，HedgeyeTech 称韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌 5%，并称台湾是最后一个破裂的 AI 泡沫，其在存储板块持有空头仓位。该机构还提到 DayOne（数据中心相关 IPO）被搁置。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123731560537149580", "2123725033272951075"]}, {"text": "对于科技板块，HedgeyeTech 表示其处境艰难，随着 2027 年科技行业前景日益不确定，“便宜”的估值可能因盈利预期被下调而变得更便宜；同时其正在研究一些更具防御性、可能抵御 AI 下行的标的 $QQQ。", "refs": ["2123732732505444862"]}], "count": 6, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@HedgeyeTech|7": {"intro": "HedgeyeTech 近期就 AI 交易降温、$ANT IPO 预期与科技板块盈利风险发表系列观点。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "HedgeyeTech 指出，AI 交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌 5%。该机构称台湾是最后一个破裂的 AI 泡沫，并表示在存储板块持有空头仓位；同时提到 DayOne（数据中心相关 IPO）被搁置。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123731560537149580", "2123725033272951075"]}, {"text": "关于 $ANT IPO，HedgeyeTech 称卖方只有买入评级，而其与投资者交流统计显示 58% 的人看空或中性、42% 看多。该机构还表示，2026 年 6 月做空 Zai（2513.HK），并就 $ANT 与 OpenAI 之间的蒸馏漏洞和全球价格战向客户发出警告；2026 年 7 月调研认为 Anthropic 增长动能已见顶、OpenAI 复苏，并平掉微软空头。", "refs": ["2123625335547998476", "2123035493226975431"]}, {"text": "HedgeyeTech 认为科技板块目前处境艰难，随着 2027 年科技行业前景日益不确定，“便宜”的估值可能因盈利预期被下调而变得更便宜。该机构表示正在研究一些更具防御性、可能抵御 AI 下行的标的 $QQQ。", "refs": ["2123732732505444862"]}], "count": 6, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@HedgeyeTech|all": {"intro": "围绕 $ANT IPO，卖方一致看多与买方调研情绪出现明显分歧，同时 AI 交易在亚洲市场承压。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "@HedgeyeTech 指出，和往常一样，卖方对 $ANT 只有买入评级；而其近期与投资者交流的统计显示，58% 的人看空或中性，42% 看多。该机构还称，2026 年 7 月根据自身调研判断 Anthropic 增长动能已见顶、OpenAI 复苏，并平掉微软空头。", "refs": ["2123625335547998476", "2123035493226975431"]}, {"text": "市场层面，该账号称 AI 交易大幅下挫，韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌 5%；并称台湾是最后一个破裂的 AI 泡沫，其在存储板块持有空头仓位，DayOne（数据中心相关 IPO）被搁置。该账号还表示，随着 2027 年科技行业前景日益不确定，“便宜”的估值可能因盈利预期被下调而变得更便宜。", "refs": ["2123607705969401895", "2123731560537149580", "2123725033272951075", "2123732732505444862"]}, {"text": "该账号回顾 2025 年所有带时间戳的多头/空头想法时称，每个想法（活跃和已关闭）的平均回报率为 16%，命中率 76%，空头想法占所有想法的 41%。", "refs": ["2008163573038715108", "2056344213776720223"]}], "count": 8, "range": "全部"}, "@Omercheema|3": {"intro": "一条推文留下的问题：复苏形态尚无答案。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "材料仅有一条推文。@Omercheema 提出“这会是V型复苏还是U型复苏？请讨论”，但未给出任何数据、时间区间或所指对象，因此无法判断其讨论的是哪一类经济或市场复苏。", "refs": ["2123862479683899849"]}], "count": 1, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@Omercheema|7": {"intro": "买方研究编辑整理 @Omercheema 近一周关于半导体估值分化与竞争机制的观察。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "@Omercheema 指出，在其跟踪的所有半导体公司里，只有 NVDA 的交易价格接近 52 周低点；许多低质量公司仍然高出 2 倍甚至 4 倍，包括 AMS、AEHR、WOLF、SIVE、AAOI 等。他同时提出“这会是V型复苏还是U型复苏？请讨论”的开放问题，并提及“五年内市值达到1.x万亿美元。惊人的成就。”", "refs": ["2123076524861432038", "2123862479683899849", "2123487859201991037"]}, {"text": "@Omercheema 以苏联解体后俄罗斯面包官员访问伦敦的故事说明协调机制：苏联由国家固定价格、委员会计划生产，短缺通过排队和配给管理；伦敦没有中央面包管理局和主食价格控制，农民、磨坊主、面包师与零售商相互竞争，结果面包充足、多样且相对便宜。他由此总结“资本主义行之有效。健康的竞争行之有效。不健康的竞争壁垒则不然。”", "refs": ["2123352600783225261"]}], "count": 9, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@Omercheema|all": {"intro": "从 Electronica 展会的短缺信号到 NVDA 的相对弱势，@Omercheema 的推文勾勒出半导体行业基本面与股价之间的张力。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "在 @Omercheema 跟踪的所有半导体公司里，只有 NVDA 的交易价格接近 52 周低点，而 AMS、AEHR、WOLF、SIVE、AAOI 等许多低质量公司仍高出 2 倍甚至 4 倍。这种分化与他在 Electronica 展会上的观察形成对照：所有品类都在短缺，且共识是情况会进一步恶化，2027 年预计会是半导体行业收入强劲的一年。", "refs": ["2123076524861432038", "2121345337986027742"]}, {"text": "@Omercheema 在 Electronica 展会上记录了几个趋势：机器人是下一个大主题，现场有数百个机器人演示；Agentic AI 正进入工程工具，西门子发布 HyperLynx Agentic Toolkit，声称在复杂高速设计上可把周期从数周缩短到数小时；欧洲面临人才短缺，预计到 2030 年半导体从业人员 30% 将退休，而新毕业生补充率不足 1%。", "refs": ["2121345337986027742"]}], "count": 10, "range": "全部"}, "@OrnnExchange|3": {"intro": "围绕算力支出与需求，@OrnnExchange 近三日给出几条观察。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "@OrnnExchange 提出一个问题：Anthropic 8,950 亿美元的算力支出，如何在其增长轨迹和盈利路径上收回？该推文称 Dario Amodei 在 CNBC 上给出了看法，并引导读者阅读其研究拆解。", "refs": ["2123811370357690494"]}, {"text": "同一账号以“算力胜过石油”作判断，并用一张图解释杰文斯悖论：代币越来越便宜，需求爆炸式增长，算力却越来越贵。这组表述把价格下降与算力成本上升并置。", "refs": ["2124177379773894895", "2123600228452360484"]}], "count": 4, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@OrnnExchange|7": {"intro": "Ornn Exchange 近一周围绕 GPU 残值、算力远期曲线与需求悖论发布多组数据与观点。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "Ornn 指出，较老的 H100 与较新的 B200、B300、GB300 的二手市场价格正在跑赢账面价值；对放贷方而言，这些 GPU 在继续产生租赁收入的同时，转售价值还能持平甚至上升，使其成为比标准五年折旧假设更强的抵押品。该机构同时发问：五年折旧安排对 GPU 残值来说是否过于悲观。", "refs": ["2123451571451167047"]}, {"text": "Ornn 已推出历史远期曲线，展示从 A100 到 GB300 的长期算力合约的历史趋势，并称算力现在也有了类似石油、天然气市场的远期曲线历史，独家收录于 Ornn Data；用户可将任意 GPU 的曲线设定到过去某个日期，或固定多个日期在同一张图表上比较。", "refs": ["2123076265359851737", "2124177379773894895"]}, {"text": "在需求侧，Ornn 以“一张图看懂杰文斯悖论”概括：代币越来越便宜，需求爆炸式增长，算力却越来越贵，并称“算力胜过石油”。此外，该机构提到 Anthropic 8,950 亿美元的算力支出，并称 Dario Amodei 在 CNBC 上就其增长轨迹和盈利路径给出看法。", "refs": ["2123600228452360484", "2124177379773894895", "2123811370357690494"]}], "count": 7, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@OrnnExchange|all": {"intro": "Ornn Exchange 近期推文围绕 GPU 残值、算力远期曲线与算力支出回报展开讨论。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "Ornn 指出，较老的 H100 与较新的 B200、B300、GB300 的二手市场价格正在跑赢账面价值；对放贷方而言，这些 GPU 在继续产生租赁收入的同时，转售价值还能持平甚至上升，使其成为比标准五年折旧假设更强的抵押品。该账号同时发问：五年折旧安排对 GPU 残值来说是否过于悲观。", "refs": ["2123451571451167047"]}, {"text": "Ornn 已推出历史远期曲线，展示从 A100 到 GB300 的长期算力合约的历史趋势，并称算力现在也有了类似石油和天然气市场长期追踪的远期曲线历史，独家收录于 Ornn Data；用户可将任意 GPU 的曲线设定到过去某个日期，或固定多个日期在同一张图表上比较。", "refs": ["2123076265359851737", "2124177379773894895"]}, {"text": "在需求与成本一侧，Ornn 称一张图看懂杰文斯悖论：代币越来越便宜，需求爆炸式增长，算力却越来越贵；该账号另提到 Anthropic 8,950 亿美元的算力支出，并称 Dario Amodei 在 CNBC 上就其如何在增长轨迹和盈利路径上收回给出了看法。", "refs": ["2123600228452360484", "2123811370357690494"]}], "count": 7, "range": "全部"}, "@RYANHINGSHING|3": {"intro": "材料仅含一条订阅者专属推文的公开预览，信息有限，以下仅就可见内容作简要梳理。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "@RYANHINGSHING 提出一个市场逻辑：Ant 上市会抽走流动性，同时波动率上升会让半导体股大跌，这次是回踩低位。该表述属于作者个人判断，并非已发生事实，且完整推文为订阅者专属，公开预览在此处中断。", "refs": ["2123787556626321770"]}], "count": 1, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@RYANHINGSHING|7": {"intro": "围绕半导体与AI模型公司，@RYANHINGSHING 近7天公开内容多为订阅预览，可核验信息有限。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "@RYANHINGSHING 提出一个观察框架：按理说，Ant 上市会抽走流动性，同时波动率上升会让半导体股大跌，这次是回踩低位；但他对 Ant 的具体判断因订阅限制未公开。该表述属其个人推测，不构成结论。", "refs": ["2123787556626321770"]}, {"text": "该作者称最近一直在研究模型公司，理由是这些公司对半导体影响很大，并提到中国 AI 模型公司似乎把战略转向 Pro，后续内容同样未公开。另有一条仅一句回应，无实质信息。", "refs": ["2123401758194184292", "2123467229903901160"]}, {"text": "在芯片销售问题上，@RYANHINGSHING 反问：英伟达在中国卖出大量芯片，你凭什么指望 AMD 不在中国卖芯片？这是其公开可见的完整观点，指向两家公司在中国市场的销售对照。", "refs": ["2124023634436235372"]}], "count": 4, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@RYANHINGSHING|all": {"intro": "围绕AI模型与算力需求，@RYANHINGSHING 近期推文呈现了其对半导体影响的思考，但多数内容为订阅者专属，公开信息有限。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "作者在11月4日推文中提到，范兄认为Post-trained开源推理模型小、Token成本小、收集优质data和eval进度慢，因此带来的算力和进度不会很快。作者认同开源推理模型市场本身很小，收入只占总体模型收入的几%。", "refs": ["2118349742426267743", "2118355323547496489"]}, {"text": "作者进一步表示，不只开源推理需求上升，闭源推理需求也上升，增速变慢是确定的。闭源推理需求很大程度来自资深工程师、研究员、量化交易员等人群，支付更多金钱不是问题，问题在于模型能力还不够强。", "refs": ["2118349742426267743"]}], "count": 6, "range": "全部"}, "@SemiAnalysis_|1": {"intro": "高通车用半导体收入快速逼近传统龙头，SemiAnalysis 认为其有望在 2027 年登顶。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 指出，九月季度高通车用业务收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元，并已超越 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美。相较 2016 年 10 月拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时 NXP 车用规模为高通的 8.6 倍，上季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增长 22 倍，到 2026 年 6 月达 650 亿美元，是 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142"]}, {"text": "路径上，高通绕开电源芯片、微控制器、模拟和传感器，切入数字座舱、ADAS 和连接，并通过收购 Arriver（2022 年）和 Autotalks（2025 年）提供软硬件平台；上季度该业务同比增长 89%，英飞凌和 NXP 仅增 10%–13%。SemiAnalysis 测算，若明年保持 12% 季度环比增长，高通将在 2027 年三季度以 28.0 亿 vs 26.8 亿美元在季度收入上超过英飞凌，全年 107 亿 vs 105 亿美元胜出。", "refs": ["2124337163357610272", "2124337165437960410"]}], "count": 7, "range": "今天"}, "@SemiAnalysis_|3": {"intro": "高通车用半导体收入快速逼近传统龙头，SemiAnalysis 认为其有望在 2027 年登顶，但节奏取决于季度增速与汇率。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 指出，高通九月季度车用业务收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元，并已超越 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美。相较 2016 年 10 月拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时 NXP 车用规模是高通的 8.6 倍，上季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，而高通单车车用收入预计从 2022 到 2026 年增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。其设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增长 22 倍，到 2026 年 6 月达 650 亿美元，是 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142"]}, {"text": "SemiAnalysis 测算，若明年保持 12% 的季度环比增长，高通将在 2027 年一季度超过 NXP，三季度在季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0 亿 vs 26.8 亿美元），并在 2027 日历年以 107 亿 vs 105 亿美元胜出；若要在 2027 财年就胜出，12 月之后需要 17.5% 的季度增速。该判断取决于季度数据和汇率。", "refs": ["2124337165437960410"]}], "count": 8, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@SemiAnalysis_|7": {"intro": "高通车用半导体收入快速逼近传统龙头，SemiAnalysis 认为其有望在 2027 年成为最大车用半导体公司。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 指出，高通车用业务收入在九月季度首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元，并已超越 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美等传统车用半导体公司。相比 2016 年 10 月高通试图以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时，NXP 车用业务规模是高通的 8.6 倍，上个季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入从 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。高通设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增长 22 倍，到 2026 年 6 月达 650 亿美元，是 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上。上季度其计算与连接业务同比增长 89%，而英飞凌和 NXP 只增长 10%–13%。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142", "2124337163357610272"]}, {"text": "SemiAnalysis 测算，若明年保持 12% 的季度环比增长，高通将在 2027 年一季度超过 NXP，三季度在季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0 亿 vs 26.8 亿美元），并在 2027 日历年胜出（107 亿 vs 105 亿美元）。若要在 2027 财年就胜出，12 月之后需要 17.5% 的季度增速。英飞凌指引 2027 财年车用业务中双位数增长，按 1.15 欧元/美元约 103 亿美元，两家公司对 12 月季度的指引都是持平。", "refs": ["2124337165437960410"]}], "count": 8, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@SemiAnalysis_|all": {"intro": "高通车用半导体收入快速逼近传统龙头，SemiAnalysis 认为其有望在 2027 年登顶。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "SemiAnalysis 指出，九月季度高通车用业务收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元，并已超越 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美。相较 2016 年 10 月高通拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时 NXP 车用规模是高通的 8.6 倍，上季度该比值已降至 1.04 倍。", "refs": ["2124337151659651116", "2124337154021101665"]}, {"text": "增长与整车销量脱钩：自 2023 年以来全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通单车车用收入 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增长 22 倍，到 2026 年 6 月达 650 亿美元，是 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上。", "refs": ["2124337156546080779", "2124337161105195142"]}, {"text": "SemiAnalysis 称，上季度高通计算与连接业务同比增长 89%，英飞凌和 NXP 只增长 10%–13%。其测算：若明年保持 12% 的季度环比增长，高通将在 2027 年三季度于季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0 亿 vs 26.8 亿美元），并在 2027 日历年以 107 亿 vs 105 亿美元胜出；若要在 2027 财年就胜出，12 月之后需要 17.5% 的季度增速。", "refs": ["2124337163357610272", "2124337165437960410"]}], "count": 8, "range": "全部"}, "@TMTLongShort|all": {"intro": "有观点认为，特朗普的贸易目标并非平衡，而是迫使盟友完全停止对华贸易。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "推文作者@TMTLongShort明确表示，特朗普的真正目标是迫使盟友彻底停止与中国的贸易，实现零进口，而非追求贸易平衡。作者强调这不是其倡导，而是掌权者所相信的。该观点认为此举旨在主动放慢中国工业崛起，并服务于储备货币地位与财政债务能力。", "refs": ["1909491586641047713"]}, {"text": "作者列举了多项风险：迫使欧洲“切腹”、习近平可能轰炸台湾晶圆厂导致全球无法获得AGI、中国抛售债券股票。同时提及特朗普顾问如Miran认为可胁迫盟友购买长期国债为安全保护伞付费，以及通过阻断中国进口解决芬太尼危机。", "refs": ["1909491586641047713"]}], "count": 1, "range": "全部"}, "@aleabitoreddit|3": {"intro": "近期AI与成长股遭遇剧烈抛售，同时供应链瓶颈与需求信号出现分歧，市场情绪极度分化。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达因SEC调查会计问题的报告下跌超12%，作者指出一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上，连带损伤冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。市场对披露与合同持久性的不信任极高，作者提出两种可能：要么过度看空创造一代人一次的AI买入机会，要么怀疑有充分理由。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2124315829202493468"]}, {"text": "需求信号矛盾：CoreWeave表示到2027年全年量化需求是算力可用性的10倍，但同一周有人主张算力过剩。全球电子协会就PCB供应链短缺发布行业警报，汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信行业报告交货时间延长，实质缓解预计在2028年中期之前。亚马逊已入股Gold Circuit Electronics确保供应，但其他行业采购未必如此。", "refs": ["2124318494879780986", "2123851594811011470"]}, {"text": "市场情绪方面，作者称所有成长型股票即便不属于AI领域，从HOOD到NBIS都像跌下悬崖，而消费必需品领域估值达到自1999年以来未见的高度。作者反问市场是否应把给予火箭或AI公司的溢价转给像沃尔玛这样的毛巾销售商。", "refs": ["2123805601411277149"]}], "count": 8, "range": "最近 3 天"}, "@aleabitoreddit|7": {"intro": "近期AI与成长股波动加剧，市场对算力需求与供应链瓶颈的认知出现明显分歧。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达因SEC调查会计问题的报告下跌超12%，作者指出一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上，连带损伤已冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。市场对披露与合同持久性的不信任极高，作者提出两种可能：要么过度看空创造一代人一次的AI买入机会，要么怀疑有充分理由。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308", "2124315829202493468"]}, {"text": "需求信号与过剩论调并存：CoreWeave表示到2027年全年量化需求是算力可用性的10倍，但同一周有人主张算力过剩并外推亚洲较小数据中心受影响。作者称这是最有趣的市场动态之一。同时，全球电子协会就PCB供应链短缺发布行业警报，称2028年中期前不太可能有实质缓解，汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信行业均报告交货时间延长。", "refs": ["2124318494879780986", "2123851594811011470"]}, {"text": "供应链紧张已波及非AI领域，关键材料短缺包括CCL和玻璃纤维布，正在挤压消费电子产品供应。作者认为短缺加剧且范围扩大，可能表明抛售开始与基本面需求脱节。此外，作者调侃民主党与特朗普均主张禁止新建数据中心，但随后澄清数据中心开发商总会找到办法完成建设，只是表态引入了不必要的不确定性。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470", "2123859267560304947", "2123841418577973727", "2123842606820135371"]}], "count": 8, "range": "最近 7 天"}, "@aleabitoreddit|all": {"intro": "英伟达会计调查传闻引发股价大跌，AI算力需求与供给的认知分歧、PCB等供应链瓶颈共同构成当日市场焦点。", "paragraphs": [{"text": "英伟达因一份新报告称SEC正调查其潜在会计问题而下跌超过12%，作者指出连带损伤已冲击主要指数和退休投资组合，并称一家市值5万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌46%以上令人错愕。", "refs": ["2123878986686333308"]}, {"text": "围绕AI算力供需，作者提到CRWV财报称到2027年全年量化需求是算力可用性的10倍，而同一周有人主张算力过剩；作者还称ORCL或SNDK/美光若能以声明安抚投资者，市场对披露和持久性的不信任极高，要么过度看空、要么怀疑有充分理由。", "refs": ["2124318494879780986", "2124315829202493468"]}, {"text": "全球电子协会就PCB供应链日益加剧的短缺发布行业警报，称汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信公司报告交货时间延长且难以确保供应，并称2028年中期前不太可能有实质缓解；作者提到CCL和玻璃纤维布短缺挤压消费电子供应，认为抛售开始与基本面需求脱节。", "refs": ["2123851594811011470"]}], "count": 8, "range": "全部"}};;
const DIGEST={"date": "2026-11-18 → 11-22", "title": "今日短评", "intro": "本期共 8 个账号、53 条推文；短评只覆盖 11-18 至 11-22 的新增内容。整体看，市场讨论集中在 AI 资产的定价与资本开支节奏上，分歧不在方向，而在时点与证据。", "paragraphs": [{"h": "一、市场情绪：龙头回落，板块未同步出清", "text": "NVDA 因一份新报告称 SEC 正在调查其潜在会计问题，单日下跌超过 **12%**，一家市值 **5 万亿美元**以上的公司几周内跌幅达 **46%** 以上，连带冲击主要指数。但板块内部并未同步调整：在 Omer Cheema 跟踪的半导体公司中，**只有 NVDA 接近 52 周低点**，多数低质量公司仍高出 **2 至 4 倍**。值得注意的两点：其一，SEC 调查目前仅有单一来源转述，未见官方确认；其二，龙头调整与板块滞涨同时存在，说明资金尚未系统性撤离。", "refs": [["aleabitoreddit", "2123878986686333308"], ["Omercheema", "2123076524861432038"]]}, {"h": "二、一级市场：发行端与二级情绪出现背离", "text": "Anthropic（$ANT）IPO 的卖方评级清一色为买入，但 Felix Wang 统计的投资者交流中，**58% 为看空或中性、42% 看多**，卖方与买方判断存在明显落差。Ornn 提出的问题更接近本质：Anthropic **8,950 亿美元**的算力支出，将以何种路径在增长与盈利上收回。发行端的乐观与买方的谨慎并存，是本轮 AI 资产定价中较值得跟踪的一组矛盾。", "refs": [["HedgeyeTech", "2123625335547998476"], ["OrnnExchange", "2123811370357690494"]]}, {"h": "三、产业动态：车用半导体的份额正在迁移", "text": "据 SemiAnalysis，高通九月季度车用收入首次接近 **20 亿美元**（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 **24.5 亿美元**与 NXP 的 **20.7 亿美元**。2016 年高通拟以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时，对方车用业务规模为其 **8.6 倍**，至上个季度该比值已降至 **1.04 倍**。其增长并非来自整车销量——全球轻型车产量自 2023 年以来基本持平——而是来自单车价值量：由 2022 年的约 **21 美元**升至 2026 年预计的 **76 美元**。", "refs": [["SemiAnalysis_", "2124337151659651116"], ["SemiAnalysis_", "2124337154021101665"], ["SemiAnalysis_", "2124337156546080779"]]}, {"h": "四、资本开支：2027 年拐点的正反证据", "text": "Freda Duan 引述腾讯 Martin Lau 的判断，认为 AI 资本开支将在 **2026-27 年见顶**，理由包括投入前置、2028 年硬件成本下降以及效率提升。与此相对，Ornn 从资产端提出不同看法：H100 与 B200、B300、GB300 的**二手市场价格正在跑赢账面价值**，五年折旧假设可能偏保守。两者讨论的并非同一问题——前者是需求节奏，后者是资产残值，但共同指向同一个变量：算力投入的回收周期。", "refs": [["FredaDuan", "2123088477868736729"], ["OrnnExchange", "2123451571451167047"]]}, {"h": "五、政策与外部变量", "text": "Felix Wang 判断**台湾是最后一个破裂的 AI 泡沫**，并自述在存储板块持有空头；同日，DayOne 的数据中心 IPO 被搁置，反映一级市场融资环境的变化。政策层面，Just Another Pod Guy 的一篇旧帖提出，关税的目标并非贸易平衡，而是迫使盟友停止对华贸易，并明确说明该表述系其对掌权者意图的推断，而非其本人主张。", "refs": [["HedgeyeTech", "2123731560537149580"], ["HedgeyeTech", "2123725033272951075"], ["TMTLongShort", "1909491586641047713"]]}, {"h": "六、后续观察", "text": "综合来看，本期材料尚不足以形成方向性结论，但留下三个可被后续数据检验的问题：一是 **2027 年前 AI 资本开支是否真的见顶**；二是 **GPU 二手价格能否继续支撑当前的折旧假设**；三是 **Anthropic 的 IPO 定价与二级市场情绪，最终由哪一侧向另一侧收敛**。三条均需等待财报、发行结果或下一轮产业调研验证。", "refs": [["FredaDuan", "2123088477868736729"], ["OrnnExchange", "2123451571451167047"], ["HedgeyeTech", "2123625335547998476"]]}], "note": "短评由编辑基于当日抓取内容撰写，每段后标注来源；文中数字均由脚本回查原文核对。本看板仅做信息整理，不构成投资建议。"};
const DATA=[{"id": "v9", "themes": ["公司"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["NVDA"], "accounts": ["aleabitoreddit"], "tweets": [{"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 2220, "r": 118, "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2123878986686333308", "en": "$NVDA drops over -12%+, from a new report that the SEC is probing potential accounting issues at Nvidia.\n\nAt this point, the collateral damage is starting to hit major indexes and retirement portfolios.\n\nIt's just wild to witness a $5T+ company crash -46%+ in weeks.", "zh": "$NVDA 下跌超过 12%，起因是一份新报告称 SEC 正在调查英伟达潜在的会计问题。\n\n到这个地步，连带损伤已经开始冲击主要指数和退休投资组合。\n\n眼睁睁看着一家市值 5 万亿美元以上的公司几周内暴跌 46% 以上，实在令人错愕。"}]}, {"id": "v8", "themes": ["公司"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["ANT"], "accounts": ["HedgeyeTech"], "tweets": [{"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "11-20", "l": 35, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/HedgeyeTech/status/2123625335547998476", "en": "As usual, only buy ratings on $ANT from sell-side. From my investors' conversations, I counted 58% bearish/neutral and 42% bullish", "zh": "和往常一样，卖方对 $ANT 只有买入评级。从我近期与投资者的交流中统计：58% 的人看空或中性，42% 看多。"}, {"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "11-18", "l": 68, "r": 5, "url": "https://x.com/HedgeyeTech/status/2123035493226975431", "en": "Today is my perspective on the $ANT IPO. I think investors have seen enough S-1 presentations, so I'm tackling Anthropic a bit differently – particularly from an AI infrastructure lens along with our robust data on global LLMs (1,130 models), conspiracy theories linking $NVDA to $ANT and my thoughts on the new BIS rule.\n\nAlso, I want to highlight two developments that we were probably the first research firm to recognize:\n\n1) June 2026 - Shorted Zai 2513.HK (China's Anthropic); warned clients on distillation loopholes from $ANT and #OpenAI, and global price war\n\n2) July 2026 - Anthropic momentum peaked according to our checks; OpenAI resurgence; removed MSFT Short\n\n（原文末尾另附完整标的清单，共 30 余个，涵盖 AI 基础设施、模型公司与中国互联网资产。）", "zh": "今天谈谈我对 $ANT IPO 的看法。我认为投资者已经看够了 S-1 路演，所以我换一种方式拆解 Anthropic——特别是从 AI 基础设施的角度，结合我们关于全球大模型（1,130 个模型）的扎实数据、把 $NVDA 与 $ANT 联系起来的各种阴谋论，以及我对新 BIS 规则的看法。\n\n另外，我想强调两个进展——我们可能是最早识别出它们的研究机构：\n\n1）2026 年 6 月——做空 Zai（2513.HK，中国的 Anthropic）；就 $ANT 与 OpenAI 之间的蒸馏漏洞和全球价格战向客户发出警告。\n\n2）2026 年 7 月——根据我们的调研，Anthropic 的增长动能已见顶；OpenAI 复苏；平掉微软空头。\n\n（原文末尾另附完整标的清单，共 30 余个，涵盖 AI 基础设施、模型公司与中国互联网资产。）"}]}, {"id": "v2", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["HedgeyeTech"], "tweets": [{"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "11-20", "l": 48, "r": 6, "url": "https://x.com/HedgeyeTech/status/2123731560537149580", "en": "Taiwan was the last AI bubble to pop. We have a memory Short there", "zh": "台湾是最后一个破裂的 AI 泡沫。我们在存储板块持有一个空头仓位。"}]}, {"id": "v1", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-22", "time": "11-22", "tickers": ["QCOM"], "accounts": ["SemiAnalysis_"], "tweets": [{"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": 217, "r": 23, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337151659651116", "en": "Is Qualcomm going to be the largest automotive semiconductor company in 2027? We think so. It’s a story the market has quietly ignored.\nIn the September quarter, Qualcomm hit nearly $2B in quarterly auto revenue for the first time ($8B annual run rate), closing in on Infineon at $2.45B and NXP at $2.07B. Qualcomm has already overtaken traditional auto semi companies such as TI, STMicro, Renesas, Analog Devices and onsemi. (1/7)", "zh": "高通会在 2027 年成为最大的车用半导体公司吗？我们认为会。这是一个被市场安静忽略的故事。\n\n在九月季度，高通的车用业务收入首次接近 20 亿美元（年化约 80 亿美元），逼近英飞凌的 24.5 亿美元和 NXP 的 20.7 亿美元。高通已经超越了 TI、意法半导体、瑞萨、ADI 和安森美等传统车用半导体公司。（1/7）"}, {"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337154021101665", "en": "Back in Oct-2016, when Qualcomm tried to buy NXP for $47B, NXP’s auto business was 8.6x the size of Qualcomm’s. Last quarter that ratio was down to 1.04x.\nEven without the NXP deal, Qualcomm went past Analog Devices in 2Q24, onsemi in 1Q25, Renesas in 4Q25, STMicro in 1Q26 and Texas Instruments in 3Q26 (by our estimate). (2/7)", "zh": "回到 2016 年 10 月，高通试图以 470 亿美元收购 NXP 时，NXP 的车用业务规模是高通的 8.6 倍。上个季度，这个比值已经降到 1.04 倍。\n\n即便没有这桩收购，高通也先后超过了 ADI（2024 年二季度）、安森美（2025 年一季度）、瑞萨（2025 年四季度）、意法半导体（2026 年一季度），以及德州仪器（2026 年三季度，按我们估算）。（2/7）"}, {"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337156546080779", "en": "Global light-vehicle production has stayed relatively flat since 2023, yet Qualcomm’s auto revenue per car is up 3.7x from 2022 to 2026E (about $21 to $76). Its auto semi growth story is decoupled from vehicle units and primarily driven by content gains. (3/7)", "zh": "自 2023 年以来，全球轻型车产量基本持平，但高通的单车车用收入从 2022 到 2026 年预计增长 3.7 倍（约从 21 美元升到 76 美元）。它的车用半导体增长与整车销量脱钩，主要由单车价值量提升驱动。（3/7）"}, {"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337159041695804", "en": "Qualcomm has beaten every auto target it has set. It guided $1.5B for fiscal 2024 and did $2.9B, guided $3.5B for fiscal 2026 and did $6.0B, and exited the year at an $8.0B annual rate five years ahead of its old fiscal 2031 goal.\nQualcomm targets $10B in auto semi revenue by fiscal 2029. If Infineon grows about 10% a year after fiscal 2027 as its CEO expects, it will reach roughly $12.4B, so Qualcomm will need to beat its target by about 25% to hold #1. (4/7)", "zh": "高通每一个车用目标都超额完成：2024 财年指引 15 亿美元、实际 29 亿；2026 财年指引 35 亿、实际 60 亿；并以 80 亿美元的年化收入收官，比原定 2031 财年目标提前了五年。\n\n高通目标 2029 财年车用半导体收入达 100 亿美元。若英飞凌按其 CEO 预期在 2027 财年后保持约 10% 年增长，将做到约 124 亿美元——高通需要超额完成目标约 25% 才能保住第一。（4/7）"}, {"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337161105195142", "en": "Qualcomm’s design-win pipeline grew 22x from $3B in early 2018 to $65B in Jun-2026, more than 2.6x Mobileye’s $24.5B pipeline.\nDriver assistance (ADAS) was already about a third of the pipeline in 2024, and BMW and Stellantis have since picked Qualcomm for central compute and driving software. Those programs start ramping in 2027 and 2028 on top of early Chinese cockpit scale. (5/7)", "zh": "高通的设计中标管线从 2018 年初的 30 亿美元增长 22 倍，到 2026 年 6 月达 650 亿美元，是 Mobileye 245 亿美元管线的 2.6 倍以上。\n\n2024 年时 ADAS 已约占管线三分之一；此后宝马和 Stellantis 又选择高通做中央计算与驾驶软件，这些项目将在 2027、2028 年放量，叠加早期中国座舱业务的规模。（5/7）"}, {"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337163357610272", "en": "Qualcomm sidestepped traditional competitors like Infineon, NXP and TI in power chips, microcontrollers, analog and sensors. It went straight after digital cockpit, ADAS and connectivity, buying Arriver (2022) for ADAS software and Autotalks (2025) for V2X safety chips to offer a complete hardware-and-software platform.\nThat compute and connectivity business grew 89% from a year ago at Qualcomm last quarter, while Infineon and NXP grew 10% to 13%. (6/7)", "zh": "高通绕开了英飞凌、NXP、TI 在电源芯片、微控制器、模拟和传感器上的正面竞争，直接切入数字座舱、ADAS 和连接，并通过收购 Arriver（2022 年，ADAS 软件）和 Autotalks（2025 年，V2X 安全芯片）提供完整的软硬件平台。\n\n上季度这块计算与连接业务同比增长 89%，而英飞凌和 NXP 只增长 10%–13%。（6/7）"}, {"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-22", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/SemiAnalysis_/status/2124337165437960410", "en": "Passing Infineon in 2027 comes down to quarterly math and FX. Infineon guided fiscal 2027 Automotive up mid-teens to roughly $10.3B at 1.15 EUR/USD (helped by moving onboard chargers into the segment), and both companies guided the December quarter flat.\n\nAt 12% quarterly growth next year (half its recent 20% to 25% pace), Qualcomm passes NXP in 1Q27, overtakes Infineon on quarterly revenue in 3Q27 ($2.80B vs $2.68B), and wins calendar 2027 ($10.7B vs $10.5B). Winning fiscal 2027 takes 17.5% quarterly growth after December. (7/7)", "zh": "2027 年能否超过英飞凌，取决于季度数据和汇率。英飞凌指引 2027 财年车用业务中双位数增长，按 1.15 欧元/美元约 103 亿美元，两家公司对 12 月季度的指引都是持平。\n\n若明年保持 12% 的季度环比增长（约为近期 20%–25% 增速的一半），高通将在 2027 年一季度超过 NXP，三季度在季度收入上超过英飞凌（28.0 亿 vs 26.8 亿美元），并在 2027 日历年胜出（107 亿 vs 105 亿美元）。若要在 2027 财年就胜出，12 月之后需要 17.5% 的季度增速。（7/7）"}]}, {"id": "v3", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-19", "time": "11-19", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["OrnnExchange"], "tweets": [{"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-19", "l": 43, "r": 8, "url": "https://x.com/OrnnExchange/status/2123451571451167047", "en": "Are five-year depreciation schedules too pessimistic on GPU residual values?\n\nAccording to Ornn Data, secondary market prices for the older H100 and the newer B200, B300 and GB300 are outpacing book value.\n\nFor lenders, these GPUs continue earning rental revenue while their resale value holds or rises, making them stronger collateral than a standard five-year schedule assumes.", "zh": "五年折旧安排对 GPU 残值来说是不是过于悲观了？\n\n根据 Ornn 的数据，较老的 H100 与较新的 B200、B300、GB300 的二手市场价格正在跑赢账面价值。\n\n对放贷方而言，这些 GPU 在继续产生租赁收入的同时，转售价值还能持平甚至上升——这使它们成为比标准五年折旧假设更强的抵押品。"}]}, {"id": "v4", "themes": ["公司", "行业"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["ANT"], "accounts": ["OrnnExchange"], "tweets": [{"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-20", "l": 22, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/OrnnExchange/status/2123811370357690494", "en": "How does Anthropic's $895 Billion in compute spend pay off for its growth trajectory and path to profitability? Dario Amodei weighs in with CNBC.\n\nRead our research for more breakdown.", "zh": "Anthropic 8,950 亿美元的算力支出，如何在其增长轨迹和盈利路径上收回？Dario Amodei 在 CNBC 上给出了看法。\n\n更多拆解请阅读我们的研究。"}]}, {"id": "v5", "themes": ["行业", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-18", "time": "11-18", "tickers": ["NVDA"], "accounts": ["Omercheema"], "tweets": [{"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-18", "l": 38, "r": 4, "url": "https://x.com/Omercheema/status/2123076524861432038", "en": "Among all semis on my tracker, Only NVDA is trading close to its 52 week low. Many low quality companies are still 2x or even 4x higher. AMS, AEHR, WOLF, SIVE, AAOI to name a few.", "zh": "在我跟踪的所有半导体公司里，只有 NVDA 的交易价格接近 52 周低点。许多低质量公司仍然高出 2 倍甚至 4 倍——AMS、AEHR、WOLF、SIVE、AAOI 等等。"}]}, {"id": "v6", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-13", "time": "11-13", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["Omercheema"], "tweets": [{"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-13", "l": 56, "r": 9, "url": "https://x.com/Omercheema/status/2121345337986027742", "en": "I was at Electronica this week. Some notes.\n\n1. Everything is in shortage, and the consensus is that conditions will worsen. 2027 is expected to be a strong year for semiconductor industry revenue. Lead times are long, and customer supply chain teams are concerned. (The decline in semiconductor stocks does not match the mood at the event, most likely because equity markets are forward-looking.)\n\n2. Robotics is clearly the next major theme. Hundreds of robotic demonstrations across the show. Many folks are now updating their profile as Physical AI experts on LinkedIn.\n\n3. Agentic AI is moving into practical engineering tools. Siemens launched the HyperLynx Agentic Toolkit for natural-language-driven signal and power integrity verification, with claimed reductions from weeks to hours on complex high-speed designs. Other EDA vendors are advancing similar agentic workflows.\n\n4. Skills and talent shortage is becoming a serious problem for Europe. 30% of semiconductor workforce in Europe is expected to retire by 2030, while new graduate input rate is less than 1%.", "zh": "本周我去了 Electronica 展会，几点笔记：\n\n1. 所有品类都在短缺，且共识是情况会进一步恶化。2027 年预计会是半导体行业收入强劲的一年。交期很长，客户的供应链团队感到担忧。（半导体股价的下跌与展会现场的情绪并不匹配，很可能是因为股市是向前看的。）\n\n2. 机器人显然是下一个大主题。展会现场有数百个机器人演示。很多人已经在 LinkedIn 上把个人简介改成「具身智能（Physical AI）专家」了。\n\n3. Agentic AI 正在进入实用的工程工具。西门子发布了 HyperLynx Agentic Toolkit，用自然语言驱动信号完整性与电源完整性验证，声称在复杂高速设计上可以把周期从数周缩短到数小时。其他 EDA 厂商也在推进类似的 agentic 工作流。\n\n4. 技能与人才短缺正在成为欧洲的严重问题。预计到 2030 年，欧洲半导体从业人员的 30% 将退休，而新毕业生的补充率不足 1%。"}]}, {"id": "v7", "themes": ["公司"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["HedgeyeTech"], "tweets": [{"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "11-20", "l": 30, "r": 2, "url": "https://x.com/HedgeyeTech/status/2123725033272951075", "en": "DayOne (data center IPO) put on hold", "zh": "DayOne（数据中心相关 IPO）被搁置。"}]}, {"id": "v10", "themes": ["行业", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-18", "time": "11-18", "tickers": ["TCEHY"], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "11-18", "l": 165, "r": 28, "url": "https://x.com/FredaDuan/status/2123088477868736729", "en": "$Tencent / Chinese CSPs' tone on the AI capex cycle is very clear -\n\nMartin Lau laid out a clear case for why AI capex should moderate after 2027:\n\n1/ Front-loaded investment: AI infrastructure is like building a factory. Once built, it can continuously train new models and generate tokens.\n\n2/ Lower hardware costs: The same equipment should cost significantly less by 2028.\n\n3/ Rapid efficiency gains: The same infrastructure can deliver exponentially more training compute and token output over time.\n\nTakeaway: Martin is effectively calling for a peak in AI capex in 2026-27, with a meaningful decline in capex intensity thereafter, even as AI demand continues to grow.\n\nThe read-through for semis is interesting: If annual industry AI capex eventually normalizes below $1T, assigning a mid-range multiple to normalized earnings, that's your industry total size.", "zh": "$Tencent / 中国云厂商对 AI 资本开支周期的口风非常清楚——\n\nMartin Lau 给出了 AI 资本开支应在 2027 年后放缓的明确理由：\n\n1/ 前置投资：AI 基础设施就像建工厂。一旦建成，就可以持续训练新模型、产出 token。\n\n2/ 硬件成本下降：到 2028 年，同样的设备成本应该会低得多。\n\n3/ 效率快速提升：同样的基础设施，随着时间推移可以输出指数级更多的训练算力和 token。\n\n结论：Martin 实际上是在说 AI 资本开支将在 2026-27 年见顶，此后资本开支强度会明显回落，即使 AI 需求仍在增长。\n\n对半导体的传导很有意思：如果行业年度 AI 资本开支最终常态化到 1 万亿美元以下，再给常态化盈利一个中位数估值倍数，那就是这个行业的总规模。"}]}, {"id": "v11", "themes": ["宏观"], "date": "2025-04-08", "time": "04-08", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["TMTLongShort"], "tweets": [{"u": "TMTLongShort", "t": "04-08", "l": 1, "r": 1806, "url": "https://x.com/TMTLongShort/status/1909491586641047713", "en": "I'll spell it out explicitly one last time.\n\nEveryone thinks Trump wants balanced trade. He does not.\n\nHe wants to force allies to stop trading with China. Completely. Zero inbound supply.\n\nBecause it's not just because of American jobs. It's a proactive move to slow down China's industrial rise.\n\nEverything is downstream of this. Reserve currency status. The ability to address fiscal debt.\n\nIt's a crazy risk because China has a vote.\n\nIt's a crazy risk because you are forcing Europe to commit seppuku because they have very little leverage or say in the matter.\n\nIt's a crazy risk because Xi might bomb the fabs in Taiwan and the world doesn't get AGI.\n\nIt's a crazy risk because China knows how financialized we are and will dump bonds and equities to drive anger towards Trump.\n\nBut it also has benefits if it works.\n\nIf your allies can't trade with China there is no near peer competitor to worry about.\n\nThat has a ton of benefits. Just look at what happened after WW2/USSR collapse when America was the last man standing.\n\nHegemony.\n\nTrump's advisors like Miran believe that you can coerce your allies to pay for your security umbrella in the form of buying longer dated treasuries.\n\nThis removes the overhangs of the debt load while allowing you to pump markets in time for midterms.\n\nIf Mexico can't import from China then you solved the fentanyl crisis because they won't have precursors.\n\nMore importantly, by establishing a tolerance for risk the level of fear you can instill in cartels is an order of magnitude higher.\n\nThis same \"logic\" applies to the Middle East.\n\nNow I will repeat for the 100x that this is not advocacy.\n\nI'm only telling you guys what the people in power believe. And I'm telling you that what happens next if I'm right will come down to how Xi wants to fight.\n\nHe can go gloves off or glove on. There are real constraints as I have outlined in prior tweets.\n\nBut there is a plan and therefore the tolerance for market pain is way way higher than you think.\n\nBecause first you need Europe to be willing to commit economic seppuku. And they won't want to (rightly). So Trump will crush them economically until they cry uncle. And then they still won't want to and he's going to threaten to defang NATO. And then they still won't want to and he will withdraw swap lines.\n\nOr a lot more likely, he will do it all very forcefully and all at once to maximize leverage.\n\nNow you'll rightly ask… why wasn't this messaged better?\n\nBecause you are attempting to execute a reckless gambit where the big variables are not what the tariffs rates are. What matters is - will Japan capitulate quickly and agree to buy a large amount of treasuries? Will Saudi capitulate quickly with your B2 bombers waiting in Diego Garcia to bomb Iran? Will China invade Taiwan?\n\nMany of you think everyone around Trump is retarded. I get it. But I will say this until I'm blue in the face. Bessent, and even Miran, have higher IQs than most if not all of you. They thought through the second order effects. If I, a dumb TMT L/S bro, thought this far ahead, they certainly did too. Which means they warned Trump how risky this was. Therefore you have to assume Trump heard the risks and said \"fuck it we ball\" anyways.\n\nEconomic Blitzkrieg. That's what we're seeing. And it's only the start.", "zh": "我最后再明确说一次。\n\n所有人都以为特朗普想要贸易平衡。他不是。\n\n他要的是迫使盟友彻底停止与中国的贸易。完全停止，零进口。\n\n因为这不只是为了美国的就业，而是一个主动放慢中国工业崛起的动作。\n\n一切都是这件事的下游：储备货币地位、解决财政债务的能力。\n\n这是个疯狂的风险，因为中国也有投票权。\n\n这是个疯狂的风险，因为你在迫使欧洲切腹——他们对这件事几乎没有筹码或话语权。\n\n这是个疯狂的风险，因为习近平可能轰炸台湾的晶圆厂，那样全世界都拿不到 AGI。\n\n这是个疯狂的风险，因为中国清楚我们金融化到什么程度，会抛售债券和股票，把怒火引向特朗普。\n\n但如果成功，也有好处。\n\n如果你的盟友不能和中国贸易，就不存在势均力敌的竞争者。\n\n这有巨大的好处。看看二战后／苏联解体后、美国成为唯一站着的人时发生了什么。\n\n霸权。\n\n特朗普的顾问如 Miran 认为，你可以胁迫盟友以购买长期国债的形式，为你的安全保护伞付费。\n\n这既消除了债务负担的悬置问题，又能赶在中期选举前托起市场。\n\n如果墨西哥不能从中国进口，你就解决了芬太尼危机，因为他们拿不到前体化学品。\n\n更重要的是，通过建立对风险的容忍度，你能向卡特尔灌输的恐惧会高一个数量级。\n\n同样的「逻辑」也适用于中东。\n\n现在我要第 100 次重申：这不是我在倡导。\n\n我只是在告诉你们掌权者在相信什么。我也在告诉你们，如果我是对的，接下来会发生什么取决于习近平想怎么打。\n\n他可以选择摘下手套，也可以戴着手套。存在真实的约束，我在之前的推文里已经列过。\n\n但确实有一套计划，因此对市场痛苦的容忍度远比你想象的高。\n\n因为首先你需要欧洲愿意经济切腹。他们不会愿意（这是对的）。所以特朗普会在经济上碾压他们，直到他们求饶。然后他们还是不愿意，他就会威胁削弱北约。然后他们还是不愿意，他就会撤回货币互换额度。\n\n或者更可能的是，他会一次性、强力地全部做出来，以最大化筹码。\n\n现在你会合理地问：为什么不把话说得更好听？\n\n因为你在执行一个鲁莽的赌局，其中关键的变量不是关税税率是多少。真正重要的是：日本会不会迅速屈服并同意购买大量国债？沙特会不会在 Diego Garcia 的 B-2 轰炸机待命时迅速屈服？中国会不会入侵台湾？\n\n你们很多人觉得特朗普身边都是弱智。我理解。但我要说到口干为止：Bessent，甚至 Miran，智商比你们大多数人（如果不是全部）都高。他们想过二阶效应。如果我这么一个蠢的 TMT 多空选手都能想到这一步，他们肯定也想到了。这意味着他们警告过特朗普这有多危险。因此你必须假设特朗普听到了风险，然后还是说「去他妈的吧，干了」。\n\n经济闪击战。这就是我们正在看到的。而这只是开始。"}]}, {"id": "v12", "themes": ["行业", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["ANT"], "accounts": ["RYANHINGSHING"], "tweets": [{"u": "RYANHINGSHING", "t": "11-20", "l": 17, "r": 0, "lang": "zh", "url": "https://x.com/RYANHINGSHING/status/2123787556626321770", "en": "按道理Ant上市會抽走流動性，同時vol上升會令半導體股大跌，今次是retest低位\n\n但我猜Ant……\n\n（此推文為訂閱者專屬內容，X 僅顯示預覽）", "zh": "按理说，Ant 上市会抽走流动性，同时波动率上升会让半导体股大跌，这次是回踩低位。\n\n但我猜 Ant……\n\n（作者设置了「订阅者专属」，完整内容需订阅才能查看，以上为 X 公开显示的预览）"}]}, {"id": "v13", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-19", "time": "11-19", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["RYANHINGSHING"], "tweets": [{"u": "RYANHINGSHING", "t": "11-19", "l": 12, "r": 0, "lang": "zh", "url": "https://x.com/RYANHINGSHING/status/2123401758194184292", "en": "最近一直在研究模型公司，因為這些公司對semi影響很大\n\n中國AI模型公司似乎把戰略投向Pro，應該……\n\n（此推文為訂閱者專屬內容，X 僅顯示預覽）", "zh": "最近一直在研究模型公司，因为这些公司对半导体影响很大。\n\n中国 AI 模型公司似乎把战略转向 Pro，应该……\n\n（作者设置了「订阅者专属」，完整内容需订阅才能查看，以上为 X 公开显示的预览）"}]}, {"id": "n1", "themes": ["行业", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["ORCL", "SNDK", "CRWV"], "accounts": ["aleabitoreddit"], "tweets": [{"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 618, "r": 39, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124315829202493468", "en": "It's very interesting \n$ORCL\n can put out statements about being fully funded for OpenAI.\n\nOr \n$SNDK\n / Micron can put out statements reassuring investors about signed LTAs + price floors. \n\nYet there's extraordinary levels of distrust toward disclosures and durability. \n\nEither everyone is excessively bearish, and this creates a generational buying opportunity on AI if contracts + projections hold... or they're skeptical for a good reason.", "zh": "$ORCL 能发布声明称已为 OpenAI 提供全额资金，这非常有意思。或者 $SNDK / 美光能发布声明，用已签署的长期协议 + 价格下限来安抚投资者。然而，市场对这些披露和持久性的不信任程度极高。要么所有人都过度看空，如果合同和预测成立，这将创造一代人一次的 AI 买入机会……要么他们怀疑是有充分理由的。"}, {"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 49, "r": 3, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124318494879780986", "en": "Maybe it's self-fufilling, we'll see. From earnings, \n$CRWV\n said 10x quantified demand > compute availability throughout 2027.\n\nThen the same week a bunch of people are arguing for a compute glut extrapolating smaller Asian DCs getting impacted. \n\nOne of the most interesting market dynamics", "zh": "也许这是自我实现的，我们拭目以待。从财报看，$CRWV 表示到 2027 年全年，量化需求是算力可用性的 10 倍。然后同一周，一群人却在主张算力过剩，并外推亚洲较小数据中心受到影响。这是最有趣的市场动态之一。"}]}, {"id": "n2", "themes": ["行业", "宏观"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["AMZN", "SPCX"], "accounts": ["aleabitoreddit"], "tweets": [{"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 378, "r": 16, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123851594811011470", "en": "I covered this earlier in Jan regarding PCB bottlenecks with photonics + \n$AMZN\n Kuiper / \n$SPCX\n starlink supply chains.\n\nBut as an update, it like other industries outside of AI are really starting to feel the pain now too.  \n\nGlobal Electronics Association: \"Is issuing this Industry Alert on escalating shortages across the printed circuit board (PCB) supply chain. \n\nCompanies in automotive, industrial, medical, defense, and telecommunications report longer lead times and difficulty securing supply as AI absorbs scarce capacity, effectively putting production at risk\"\n\nThe association meaningful relief unlikely before mid-2028. The association urged buyers to plan ahead for supply constraints and manufacturers.\n\nHyperscalers like \n$AMZN\n already planned ahead of time taking stakes in Gold Circuit Electronics (2368) for supply procurement... \n\nBut can't say the same about other industries procurement (medical industry is probably not used to competing with hyperscalers over the same supply lol). \n\nThe resulting shortages of critical materials, including CCLs and fibreglass cloth, are squeezing supplies for consumer electronics.\n\nTLDR: same bottleneck, same timeline for 2028. It's just interesting to see association warnings about it impacting medical to defense industries. \n\nSo there's incremental information that it's become an industry wide allocation issue. \n\nI also think it's helpful to see escalating shortages + broadening... so it might show the selloff is starting to look very disconnected with fundamental demand.", "zh": "我在1月份早些时候就报道过PCB瓶颈与光子学+ $AMZN Kuiper / $SPCX 星链供应链的问题。\n\n但作为更新，它和AI以外的其他行业一样，现在也真的开始感受到痛苦了。\n\n全球电子协会：“就印刷电路板（PCB）供应链日益加剧的短缺发布此行业警报。\n\n汽车、工业、医疗、国防和电信行业的公司报告称，随着AI吸收稀缺产能，交货时间延长且难以确保供应，实际上使生产面临风险”\n\n该协会表示，在2028年中期之前不太可能有实质性的缓解。该协会敦促买家提前规划供应限制和制造商。\n\n像 $AMZN 这样的超大规模企业已经提前规划，入股Gold Circuit Electronics（2368）以确保供应采购……\n\n但不能说其他行业的采购也是如此（医疗行业可能不习惯与超大规模企业在同一供应上竞争，哈哈）。\n\n由此产生的关键材料短缺，包括CCL和玻璃纤维布，正在挤压消费电子产品的供应。\n\nTLDR：同样的瓶颈，2028年的同样时间线。看到协会警告其影响从医疗到国防行业，这很有趣。\n\n因此有增量信息表明，这已成为一个全行业范围的分配问题。\n\n我还认为，看到短缺加剧+范围扩大是有帮助的……因此这可能表明抛售开始看起来与基本面需求非常脱节。"}, {"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 71, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123859267560304947", "en": "Thanks, I'll try to make more higher signal fundamental posts. I tend to post more random stuff when I'm stressed (especially with the broader market crash)\n\nBut it is pretty wild to see the disconnect between supply procurement patterns and valuations during this deleveraging period.", "zh": "但更新一下，像其他非AI行业现在也开始真正感受到痛苦了。"}]}, {"id": "n3", "themes": ["宏观", "行业"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["CRWV"], "accounts": ["aleabitoreddit"], "tweets": [{"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 1300, "r": 68, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123841418577973727", "en": "> Democrats: \"Let's ban new datacenters in the US\"\n> Trump: \"Let's ban new datacenters overseas\"\n> \n$CRWV\n: ???", "zh": "民主党人：“让我们在美国禁止新建数据中心”\n特朗普：“让我们在海外禁止新建数据中心”\n$CRWV：？？？"}, {"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 63, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123842606820135371", "en": "It's much more nuanced than that, I'm just making a joke. DC developers will find ways to get it done.\n\nIt's just statements from Trump like this introduce unnecessary uncertainty.", "zh": "实际情况要微妙得多，我只是开个玩笑。数据中心开发商总会找到办法完成建设。\n只是特朗普这样的表态引入了不必要的不确定性。"}]}, {"id": "n4", "themes": ["宏观", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["HOOD", "NBIS"], "accounts": ["aleabitoreddit"], "tweets": [{"u": "aleabitoreddit", "t": "11-20", "l": 1700, "r": 93, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123805601411277149", "en": "Feels like every growth equity, even outside of AI, from \n$HOOD\n to \n$NBIS\n has fallen off a cliff.\n\nMeanwhile bubbles are forming in consumer staples, with valuations not seen since 1999.\n\nDo you guys think markets are right... that premiums given to rocket or AI companies, should be given to towel resellers like Walmart instead?", "zh": "感觉所有成长型股票，即便不属于AI领域，从$HOOD到$NBIS，都像是跌下了悬崖。\n\n与此同时，消费必需品领域正在形成泡沫，估值达到了自1999年以来未见的高度。\n\n你们认为市场是对的……即给予火箭或AI公司的溢价，应该转而给予像沃尔玛这样的毛巾销售商吗？"}]}, {"id": "n5", "themes": ["公司"], "date": "2026-11-21", "time": "11-21", "tickers": ["NVDA", "AMD"], "accounts": ["SemiAnalysis_"], "tweets": [{"u": "SemiAnalysis_", "t": "11-21", "l": 791, "r": 49, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124267194267652470", "en": "BREAKING: Jensen Huang reportedly told NVIDIA employees that if AMD's Minimax Inferact kernels beat NVIDIA's on AgentX performance targets, he would reset every NVIDIA employee's GTA 6 progress.\n\nThe employees then broke down crying. Jensen called it \"high-performance levers of motivation.\"\n\nIs this the kind of thing you want to see from the leader of one of the largest companies on Earth? Disgusting. (Source: roommate)", "zh": "突发：据报道，黄仁勋对NVIDIA员工表示，如果AMD的Minimax Inferact内核在AgentX性能目标上击败NVIDIA，他将重置每位NVIDIA员工的GTA 6进度。\n\n员工们随后痛哭失声。黄仁勋称之为“高性能激励杠杆”。\n\n这是你想从地球上最大公司之一的领导者身上看到的事情吗？令人作呕。（来源：室友）"}]}, {"id": "n6", "themes": ["宏观"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["Omercheema"], "tweets": [{"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-20", "l": 25, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123862479683899849", "en": "Is it going to be a V shaped recovery or U shaped? Discuss", "zh": "这会是V型复苏还是U型复苏？请讨论"}]}, {"id": "n7", "themes": ["宏观"], "date": "2026-11-19", "time": "11-19", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["Omercheema"], "tweets": [{"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-19", "l": 17, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123487859201991037", "en": "1.x trillion market cap  in 5 years. Amazing achievement.", "zh": "五年内市值达到1.x万亿美元。惊人的成就。"}, {"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-19", "l": 28, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123352600783225261", "en": "In 1990s, shortly after the Soviet Union collapsed, a Russian official responsible for bread production visited London. Standing in shops stocked with fresh loaves of every variety, he asked his British hosts: who was in charge of the bread supply for the entire city?\n\nThe answer “nobody” left him stunned. In the Soviet Union,  Prices were fixed by the state, production was planned by committees, and shortages were managed through queues and rationing. Officials spent endless hours calculating how many loaves should be baked each day, yet the result was frequently too little, too much, or the wrong kind. \n\nIn London there was no central bakery directorate, no daily conference of factory managers reporting to a ministry, and no price controls on the staple. Farmers, millers, bakers, and retailers simply competed. Each sought a profit; none coordinated by decree. The outcome was abundant, varied, and relatively inexpensive bread available on demand. The official could not immediately accept that this unplanned coordination, driven by price signals rather than commands, had solved a problem that central planning had never mastered.\n\nCapitalism works. Healthy competition works. Unhealthy barriers to competition don't.", "zh": "上世纪90年代，苏联解体后不久，一位负责面包生产的俄罗斯官员访问了伦敦。站在摆满各种新鲜面包的商店里，他问英国东道主：谁负责整个城市的面包供应？\n\n“没有人”这个回答让他震惊。在苏联，价格由国家固定，生产由委员会计划，短缺通过排队和配给来管理。官员们花费无数时间计算每天应该烤多少面包，但结果常常是太少、太多或种类不对。\n\n在伦敦，没有中央面包管理局，没有工厂经理每天向部委汇报的会议，也没有对主食的价格控制。农民、磨坊主、面包师和零售商只是相互竞争。每个人都追求利润；没有人靠法令协调。结果是充足、多样且相对便宜的面包随需可得。这位官员无法立即接受，这种由价格信号而非命令驱动的无计划协调，解决了一个中央计划从未掌握的问题。\n\n资本主义行之有效。健康的竞争行之有效。不健康的竞争壁垒则不然。"}]}, {"id": "n8", "themes": ["宏观"], "date": "2026-11-19", "time": "11-19", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["Omercheema"], "tweets": [{"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-19", "l": 20, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123408274623975710", "en": "Happy Anthropic Day. \n\nMay Lakshmi devi bless you all.", "zh": "人类学日快乐。愿拉克希米女神保佑你们所有人。"}, {"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-19", "l": 28, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123352600783225261", "en": "In 1990s, shortly after the Soviet Union collapsed, a Russian official responsible for bread production visited London. Standing in shops stocked with fresh loaves of every variety, he asked his British hosts: who was in charge of the bread supply for the entire city?\n\nThe answer “nobody” left him stunned. In the Soviet Union,  Prices were fixed by the state, production was planned by committees, and shortages were managed through queues and rationing. Officials spent endless hours calculating how many loaves should be baked each day, yet the result was frequently too little, too much, or the wrong kind. \n\nIn London there was no central bakery directorate, no daily conference of factory managers reporting to a ministry, and no price controls on the staple. Farmers, millers, bakers, and retailers simply competed. Each sought a profit; none coordinated by decree. The outcome was abundant, varied, and relatively inexpensive bread available on demand. The official could not immediately accept that this unplanned coordination, driven by price signals rather than commands, had solved a problem that central planning had never mastered.\n\nCapitalism works. Healthy competition works. Unhealthy barriers to competition don't.", "zh": "上世纪90年代，苏联解体后不久，一位负责面包生产的俄罗斯官员访问了伦敦。站在摆满各种新鲜面包的商店里，他问英国东道主：谁负责整个城市的面包供应？\n\n“没有人”这个回答让他震惊。在苏联，价格由国家固定，生产由委员会计划，短缺通过排队和配给来管理。官员们花费无数时间计算每天应该烤多少面包，但结果常常是太少、太多或种类不对。\n\n在伦敦，没有中央面包管理局，没有工厂经理每天向部委汇报的会议，也没有对主食的价格控制。农民、磨坊主、面包师和零售商只是相互竞争。每个人都追求利润；没有人靠法令协调。结果是充足、多样且相对便宜的面包随需可得。这位官员无法立即接受，这种由价格信号而非命令驱动的无计划协调，解决了一个中央计划从未掌握的问题。\n\n资本主义行之有效。健康的竞争行之有效。不健康的竞争壁垒则不然。"}]}, {"id": "n9", "themes": ["宏观"], "date": "2026-11-18", "time": "11-18", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["Omercheema"], "tweets": [{"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-18", "l": 17, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123353742871310697", "en": "Nobody knows the future. Nothing wrong with revisiting estimates. Analysts do it wll the time.", "zh": "没人知道未来。重新审视估算没有错。分析师们一直这么做。"}, {"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-18", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123434160891089373", "en": "Yes. ", "zh": "是的。"}, {"u": "Omercheema", "t": "11-18", "l": 28, "r": 1, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123352600783225261", "en": "In 1990s, shortly after the Soviet Union collapsed, a Russian official responsible for bread production visited London. Standing in shops stocked with fresh loaves of every variety, he asked his British hosts: who was in charge of the bread supply for the entire city?\n\nThe answer “nobody” left him stunned. In the Soviet Union,  Prices were fixed by the state, production was planned by committees, and shortages were managed through queues and rationing. Officials spent endless hours calculating how many loaves should be baked each day, yet the result was frequently too little, too much, or the wrong kind. \n\nIn London there was no central bakery directorate, no daily conference of factory managers reporting to a ministry, and no price controls on the staple. Farmers, millers, bakers, and retailers simply competed. Each sought a profit; none coordinated by decree. The outcome was abundant, varied, and relatively inexpensive bread available on demand. The official could not immediately accept that this unplanned coordination, driven by price signals rather than commands, had solved a problem that central planning had never mastered.\n\nCapitalism works. Healthy competition works. Unhealthy barriers to competition don't.", "zh": "上世纪90年代，苏联解体后不久，一位负责面包生产的俄罗斯官员访问了伦敦。站在摆满各种新鲜面包的商店里，他问英国东道主：谁负责整个城市的面包供应？\n\n“没有人”这个回答让他震惊。在苏联，价格由国家制定，生产由委员会计划，短缺通过排队和配给来管理。官员们花费无数时间计算每天应该烤多少面包，但结果常常是太少、太多或种类不对。\n\n在伦敦，没有中央面包管理局，没有工厂经理每天向部委汇报的会议，也没有对主食的价格控制。农民、磨坊主、面包师和零售商只是相互竞争。每个人都追求利润；没有人靠法令协调。结果是充足、多样且相对便宜的面包随需供应。这位官员无法立即接受，这种由价格信号而非命令驱动的无计划协调，解决了一个中央计划从未掌握的问题。\n\n资本主义行之有效。健康的竞争行之有效。不健康的竞争壁垒则不然。"}]}, {"id": "n10", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-21", "time": "11-21", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["OrnnExchange"], "tweets": [{"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-21", "l": 57, "r": 7, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124177379773894895", "en": "\"Compute beats oil.\"\n\nOur co-founder & CEO \n@Bavaria_kush\n sat down with \n@HarryStebbings\n on \n@20VC\n to talk about the state of compute and AI.\n\nWatch the full episode: \nhttps://\nyoutu.be/3ZkDiDrxDeY", "zh": "算力胜过石油。"}]}, {"id": "n11", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["OrnnExchange"], "tweets": [{"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-20", "l": 55, "r": 4, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123600228452360484", "en": "Jevons paradox in one chart: tokens get cheaper, demand explodes, compute gets pricier. \n\nWe track both, every day on Ornn Data.", "zh": "一张图看懂杰文斯悖论：代币越来越便宜，需求爆炸式增长，算力却越来越贵。"}]}, {"id": "n12", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-18", "time": "11-18", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["OrnnExchange"], "tweets": [{"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-18", "l": 81, "r": 8, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123076265359851737", "en": "Ornn has launched Historical Forward Curves, showing historical trends in long-term compute contracts from A100 to GB300.\n\nMature markets like oil and natural gas have long tracked the history of their forward curves to benchmark prices and manage term risk. Compute now has this history too, exclusively on Ornn Data.\n\nSet any GPU’s curve to a past date, or pin several dates and compare them on one chart, to see how prices moved before you lock a contract.\n\nExplore the curves → \nhttp://\ndata.ornn.com/analytics", "zh": "Ornn 已推出历史远期曲线，展示从 A100 到 GB300 的长期算力合约的历史趋势。\n\n像石油和天然气这样的成熟市场长期以来一直追踪其远期曲线的历史，以对标价格并管理期限风险。算力现在也有了这样的历史，独家收录于 Ornn Data。\n\n将任意 GPU 的曲线设定到过去的某个日期，或固定多个日期并在同一张图表上进行比较，以便在锁定合约之前查看价格是如何变动的。\n\n探索这些曲线 → \nhttp://\ndata.ornn.com/analytics"}, {"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-18", "l": 57, "r": 7, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124177379773894895", "en": "\"Compute beats oil.\"\n\nOur co-founder & CEO \n@Bavaria_kush\n sat down with \n@HarryStebbings\n on \n@20VC\n to talk about the state of compute and AI.\n\nWatch the full episode: \nhttps://\nyoutu.be/3ZkDiDrxDeY", "zh": "像石油和天然气这样的成熟市场长期以来一直追踪其远期曲线的历史，以基准价格和管理期限风险。算力现在也有了这样的历史，独家在Ornn Data上提供。"}]}, {"id": "n13", "themes": ["公司"], "date": "2026-01-05", "time": "01-05", "tickers": ["NVDA", "CRWV", "NBIS", "SE"], "accounts": ["HedgeyeTech"], "tweets": [{"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "01-05", "l": 68, "r": 10, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2008163573038715108", "en": "Cheers to a happy & healthy 2026! Below are all timestamped Long/Short ideas for 2025 and vs respective benchmarks. Appreciate everyone's support.\n\nOur average return per idea (active & closed ideas) is 16%. 76% hit rate. Short ideas accounted for 41% of all ideas.\n\nFor tech research subscription, see below. We're adding a new product in 2026, geared for traders. Stay tuned.   \n\nhttps://\ninsights.hedgeye.com/global-tech-fe\nlix-wang/\n…\n\n\n$NVDA\n \n$CRWV\n \n$NBIS\n \n$SE\n \n$BABA\n $TCEHY \n$AAPL\n \n$POET\n \n$ONTO\n \nhttp://\n5930.KR \n$MU\n $DIDIY \n$SITM\n \n$MNSO\n \n$WYFI\n $MPNGY $XIACY \n$VRT\n \n$VRNS\n \n$PDD\n \n$AMAT", "zh": "为2026年的幸福与健康干杯！以下是2025年所有带时间戳的多头/空头想法及与各自基准的对比。感谢大家的支持。\n\n我们每个想法（活跃和已关闭的想法）的平均回报率为16%。命中率为76%。空头想法占所有想法的41%。\n\n关于科技研究订阅，请见下文。我们将在2026年推出一款面向交易者的新产品。敬请关注。\n\nhttps://\ninsights.hedgeye.com/global-tech-fe\nlix-wang/\n…\n\n\n$NVDA\n \n$CRWV\n \n$NBIS\n \n$SE\n \n$BABA\n $TCEHY \n$AAPL\n \n$POET\n \n$ONTO\n \nhttp://\n5930.KR \n$MU\n $DIDIY \n$SITM\n \n$MNSO\n \n$WYFI\n $MPNGY $XIACY \n$VRT\n \n$VRNS\n \n$PDD\n \n$AMAT"}, {"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "01-05", "l": null, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2056344213776720223", "en": "Global Tech Pro Sector product", "zh": "我们每个想法（活跃和已关闭）的平均回报为16%。命中率76%。空头想法占所有想法的41%。"}]}, {"id": "n14", "themes": ["宏观", "行业"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": ["QQQ"], "accounts": ["HedgeyeTech"], "tweets": [{"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "11-20", "l": 75, "r": 2, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123732732505444862", "en": "Tough spot for tech right now. With an increasingly uncertain 2027 for tech, “cheap” valuations could get cheaper as estimates get cut. On the other hand, I’m looking into more insulated plays that may  withstand AI downturns  \n$QQQ", "zh": "科技板块目前处境艰难。随着2027年科技行业前景日益不确定，\"便宜\"的估值可能因盈利预期被下调而变得更便宜。另一方面，我正在研究一些更具防御性、可能抵御AI下行的标的 $QQQ"}]}, {"id": "n15", "themes": ["宏观", "行业"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["HedgeyeTech"], "tweets": [{"u": "HedgeyeTech", "t": "11-20", "l": 57, "r": 3, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123607705969401895", "en": "AI trade plummeting - Korea, Japan and Taiwan indexes all down 5% overnight.", "zh": "AI 交易大幅下挫——韩国、日本和台湾股指隔夜均下跌 5%。"}]}, {"id": "n16", "themes": ["行业", "行业"], "date": "2026-11-04", "time": "11-04", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["RYANHINGSHING"], "tweets": [{"u": "RYANHINGSHING", "t": "11-04", "l": 33, "r": 6, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2118349742426267743", "en": "我昨天指\"Post-training是下一波算力浪潮\"引起了范總和金老師的辯論。我就無意跟任何人辯論了，只是思考了一天，有空就想說下我都想法。\n\n范兄說的話有道理。他指Post-trained開源推理模型小、Token成本小、收集優質data和eval進度慢，所以Post-trained模型帶來的算力和進度也不會很快(應該是和之前AI coding增長相比)。\n\n確實如此，開源推理模型市場本身真的很小，收入只佔總體模型收入的幾%。所以即使開源有明顯增長，可能未來一年都不會為整體算力帶來明顯的增長。而且不能忽視優質data和eval等瓶頸。\n\n我的看法是\n1. 不只開源推理需求在上升，閉源推理需求也上升（增速變慢是確定的）。閉源推理需求很大程度上來自資深工程師、研究員、量化交易員、...等人的需求。對於這部分人來說，支付更多金錢從來不是問題，問題出在模型能力還不夠強，有不低的錯誤率和需要人工 review。模型還在進步當中，所以閉源推理需求上升是確定的。\n\n2. Post-trained開源推理模型增速高於閉源推理增速，這是企業應用AI在workflow的關鍵。當workflow產生又同時帶動非傳統coding更複雜的AI需求(例如code review、security、testing、product design、 ...)\n\n3. 很多人非常看重ROI，但很多公司都不是看ROI，而是看有沒有被新玩家顛覆的風險， token spending作用風險管理策略。\n\n所以未來需求還是會大幅增長，問題從來是需求增速下降會不會導致供大於需。以我找到CSP的渠道，他們有信心2-3年算力繼續供不應求。即使需求增速變慢，供應依然是瓶頸。\n\n對我來說唯一問題是雲能不能維持 >$ 50B/GW以上的暴利收入。我看法是GW收入不一定維持，但是整體半導體和算力依然供不應求。\n\n范兄認為算力和半導體是週期性(下跌)的，長期看好AI，我表示尊重。我認為或許只有部分半導體公司的需求會面臨週期性下跌，會繼續缺貨的還是會繼續缺貨。", "zh": "我昨天指\"Post-training是下一波算力浪潮\"引起了范總和金老師的辯論。我就無意跟任何人辯論了，只是思考了一天，有空就想說下我都想法。\n\n范兄說的話有道理。他指Post-trained開源推理模型小、Token成本小、收集優質data和eval進度慢，所以Post-trained模型帶來的算力和進度也不會很快(應該是和之前AI coding增長相比)。\n\n確實如此，開源推理模型市場本身真的很小，收入只佔總體模型收入的幾%。所以即使開源有明顯增長，可能未來一年都不會為整體算力帶來明顯的增長。而且不能忽視優質data和eval等瓶頸。\n\n我的看法是\n1. 不只開源推理需求在上升，閉源推理需求也上升（增速變慢是確定的）。閉源推理需求很大程度上來自資深工程師、研究員、量化交易員、...等人的需求。對於這部分人來說，支付更多金錢從來不是問題，問題出在模型能力還不夠強，有不低的錯誤率和需要人工 review。模型還在進步當中，所以閉源推理需求上升是確定的。\n\n2. Post-trained開源推理模型增速高於閉源推理增速，這是企業應用AI在workflow的關鍵。當workflow產生又同時帶動非傳統coding更複雜的AI需求(例如code review、security、testing、product design、 ...)\n\n3. 很多人非常看重ROI，但很多公司都不是看ROI，而是看有沒有被新玩家顛覆的風險， token spending作用風險管理策略。\n\n所以未來需求還是會大幅增長，問題從來是需求增速下降會不會導致供大於需。以我找到CSP的渠道，他們有信心2-3年算力繼續供不應求。即使需求增速變慢，供應依然是瓶頸。\n\n對我來說唯一問題是雲能不能維持 >$ 50B/GW以上的暴利收入。我看法是GW收入不一定維持，但是整體半導體和算力依然供不應求。\n\n范兄認為算力和半導體是週期性(下跌)的，長期看好AI，我表示尊重。我認為或許只有部分半導體公司的需求會面臨週期性下跌，會繼續缺貨的還是會繼續缺貨。"}, {"u": "RYANHINGSHING", "t": "11-04", "l": 4, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2118355323547496489", "en": "補充：供需沒預期中緊張也是一種利潤不及預期的風險，不一定是需求下跌帶來的利潤風險", "zh": "范兄说的话有道理。他指Post-trained开源推理模型小、Token成本小、收集优质data和eval进度慢，所以Post-trained模型带来的算力和进度也不会很快（应该是和之前AI coding增长相比）。"}]}, {"id": "n17", "themes": ["行业"], "date": "2026-11-19", "time": "11-19", "tickers": ["AMD", "NVDA"], "accounts": ["RYANHINGSHING"], "tweets": [{"u": "RYANHINGSHING", "t": "11-19", "l": 14, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123467229903901160", "en": "You don’t say…\n\nWhy do you expect that \n$AMD\n doesn’t sell chips in China when \n$NVDA\n sells lots of chips in China?", "zh": "可不是嘛……"}, {"u": "RYANHINGSHING", "t": "11-19", "l": 4, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124023634436235372", "en": "壽司郎太多人排隊了\n\n事已至此，去食海南雞飯\n\n@on8482669519610\n  \nhttps://\nx.com/on848266951961\n/on8482669519610/status/2124023634436235372\n…", "zh": "英伟达在中国卖出大量芯片，你凭什么指望AMD不在中国卖芯片？"}]}, {"id": "n18", "themes": ["行业", "行业"], "date": "2026-11-22", "time": "11-22", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "11-22", "l": 85, "r": 11, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2124325047120900224", "en": "RSI is a powerful deflationary flywheel: compounding gains in token efficiency drive down the compute required to deliver the same level of intelligence. Token consumption, model revenue, and semiconductor demand are three very different things - yet the market often treats them as the same trade.\n\nThe cost of intelligence is already falling at an extraordinary pace.\n\nEpoch AI estimates that the cost of achieving a fixed level of AI capability has declined ~47% per quarter since 2023. Separately, research on model capability density suggests that comparable performance can be delivered with roughly half the parameters every 3.5 months. Capabilities that once required frontier-scale models are increasingly available in much smaller, cheaper models.\n\nRSI could accelerate this trend even further. The faster intelligence improves, the faster it may become cheaper to produce. AI capabilities could advance exponentially without requiring a proportional increase in compute.\n\nThis creates an increasingly demanding hurdle for growth.\n\nAt a 47% quarterly decline in the cost of a fixed level of intelligence, consumption of that intelligence would need to increase ~90% per quarter just to keep the associated revenue flat, all else equal. New use cases and economically valuable workloads must be unlocked fast enough to absorb that deflation.\n\nSo far, demand growth has been extraordinary. OpenRouter processed nearly 25x more tokens in October than in January, while effective token prices fell 57-70% over the same period. But exponential token growth does not automatically translate into exponential revenue growth, let alone sustained growth in semiconductor capex.\n\nFor the past several years, rapid advances in frontier AI, explosive token consumption, and accelerating infrastructure investment have largely reinforced one another.\n\nThere is no guarantee these three curves will continue to move together.\n\nThe next phase of AI will be defined not just by how quickly intelligence improves, but by whether new demand can outrun the deflation that comes with that progress.\n\n—\n\nEpoch AI - The Plunging Price of Thought\n\nhttps://\nepoch.ai/publications/t\nhe-plunging-price-of-thought\n…\n\nNature Machine Intelligence - Densing Law of LLMs\n\nhttps://\nnature.com/articles/s4225\n6-025-01137-0\n…\n\nOpenRouter - October 2026 Data Recap\n\nhttps://\nopenrouter.ai/data/october-2\n026\n…", "zh": "RSI是一个强大的通缩飞轮：代币效率的复合增益推动降低提供同等智能水平所需的算力。代币消耗、模型收入和半导体需求是三件截然不同的事情——然而市场往往将它们视为同一笔交易。\n\n智能的成本已经在以非凡的速度下降。\n\nEpoch AI估计，自2023年以来，实现固定水平AI能力的成本每季度下降约47%。另外，关于模型能力密度的研究表明，大约每3.5个月就可以用大约一半的参数提供可比性能。曾经需要前沿规模模型才能实现的能力，正越来越多地出现在小得多、便宜得多的模型中。\n\nRSI可能会进一步加速这一趋势。智能提升得越快，其生产成本可能下降得越快。AI能力可能会指数级进步，而不需要算力成比例增加。\n\n这为增长创造了一个日益苛刻的门槛。\n\n在固定水平智能的成本每季度下降47%的情况下，其他条件不变时，对这种智能的消耗需要每季度增长约90%，才能仅保持相关收入持平。新的用例和有经济价值的工作负载必须足够快地解锁，以吸收这种通缩。\n\n到目前为止，需求增长非同寻常。OpenRouter在10月处理的代币量几乎是1月的25倍，而同期有效代币价格下降了57-70%。但代币的指数级增长并不会自动转化为收入的指数级增长，更不用说半导体资本支出的持续增长。\n\n过去几年，前沿AI的快速进步、代币消耗的爆炸式增长以及基础设施投资的加速，在很大程度上相互强化。\n\n不能保证这三条曲线会继续一起移动。\n\nAI的下一阶段不仅将由智能提升的速度来定义，还将由新需求能否跑赢伴随这一进步而来的通缩来定义。\n\n—\n\nEpoch AI - 思维价格的暴跌\n\nhttps://\nepoch.ai/publications/t\nhe-plunging-price-of-thought\n…\n\nNature Machine Intelligence - 大语言模型的致密化定律\n\nhttps://\nnature.com/articles/s4225\n6-025-01137-0\n…\n\nOpenRouter - 2026年10月数据回顾\n\nhttps://\nopenrouter.ai/data/october-2\n026\n…"}]}, {"id": "n19", "themes": ["行业", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-10", "time": "11-10", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "11-10", "l": 25, "r": 3, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2120214931731775587", "en": "Congrats to \n@QuanquanGu\n and the Geodesic Intelligence team on the launch of NovaAtom-Lite!\n\nParticularly impressive to see what a small team has been able to accomplish in just a few months. Based on the reported results, NovaAtom-Lite appears to outperform Isomorphic Labs’ IsoDDE and Google DeepMind’s AlphaFold 3 on this specific antibody-antigen structure prediction benchmark.\n\nA great example of how a focused team with strong technical talent can move quickly and push the boundaries. \n\nExcited to see progress on AI drug discovery!", "zh": "祝贺@QuanquanGu和Geodesic Intelligence团队推出NovaAtom-Lite！\n\n尤其令人印象深刻的是，一个小团队在短短几个月内就能取得这样的成果。根据报告的结果，在这个特定的抗体-抗原结构预测基准上，NovaAtom-Lite似乎优于Isomorphic Labs的IsoDDE和Google DeepMind的AlphaFold 3。\n\n这是一个很好的例子，说明一支拥有强大技术人才的专注团队能够快速行动并推动边界。\n\n很高兴看到AI药物发现的进展！"}]}, {"id": "n20", "themes": ["行业", "行业"], "date": "2026-10-26", "time": "10-26", "tickers": ["TSLA"], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "10-26", "l": 1100, "r": 237, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2114772074438988256", "en": "10 Spicy Takes After Talking to 50 Friends at the Frontier of Robotics \n\n1/ Astra IS robotics' GPT-3 moment. Ironically, now that it's finally here, some in robotics seem reluctant to acknowledge it. Perhaps because it (sadly) didn't come from a robotics company?\n\n2/ Robotics is becoming just another vertical for frontier labs. Not so different from coding in some respects. Why reinvent general intelligence for every industry?\n\n3/ Robotics was too hard to underwrite until now. No convincing pretraining scaling law, no convergence on models, data, or hardware. No wonder some critics dismissed it as a fragmented industry playing an expensive \"demo game\". Astra may finally offer a credible path to scale.\n\n4/ Robotics foundation-model startups have a case. But how strong is it? The argument: Astra handles System 2 (reasoning), while specialized models retain System 1 (skills) and System 0 (motor control). Fair. But isn't that already a narrower value proposition? And who says the boundary stops there?\n\n5/ Follow the talent. Word is OpenAI reorganized its 30–40-person robotics team around the core Astra model. Hearing similar moves toward general models at \n@Tesla_Optimus\n. Org charts may tell us more than any demo.\n\n6/ The robotics data gold rush is real. Million-hour procurement programs, some potentially reaching tens of millions of hours. Talk of budgets approaching $1B per frontier lab.\n\n7/ Bullish on robotics hardware volumes. As intelligence becomes more accessible, the barriers to building useful robots could fall dramatically. The moat shifts toward reliability, dexterity, integration, and deployment.\n\n8/ Robotics could fuel the next semiconductor and memory supercycle. A 100B-parameter model running on the edge requires ~50GB just for 4-bit weights. Now multiply that by millions of robots. Why do you think \n@JensenHuang\n is so obsessed with robotics? \n@elonmusk\n saw it coming: \nhttps://\nx.com/elonmusk/statu\ns/2114772074438988256?a=ZJpCuCM8Iv8RkRR_g_A&s=20\n…\n\n9/ Is self-driving immune to the general-model threat? After coding and robotics, why assume self-driving remains the exclusive domain of proprietary, vertical models? Robotaxi increasingly feels like a solved problem to me. But if and when frontier labs move into self-driving, we could see an Apple vs. Android dynamic. Think about the implications for \n$TSLA\n, Waymo, and other OEMs.\n\n10/ The next bottleneck may not be intelligence. It's deployment. Models are improving faster than our ability to deploy robots in the messy real world. Integration, hardware variance, failure recovery, and economics remain brutally hard. The real moat may be turning intelligence into reliable, profitable physical work.\n\n--\nI realize some of these takes may rub people the wrong way, especially those who have spent years doing the hard work of advancing robotics. That's not my intention. \n\nI'm sharing them to spark debate, not to declare winners and losers. Astra has only been out for a month or so, and it's far too early to draw definitive conclusions. More importantly, when the TAM is this enormous - potentially the largest in tech - there should be plenty of room for different approaches and many winners.\n\n++\nFull diligence report: \nhttps://\nrobonomics.substack.com/p/robotics-new\n-era-after-astra?r=3hcp4&utm_campaign=post&utm_medium=web\n…", "zh": "与50位机器人前沿领域的朋友交谈后的10个辛辣观点\n\n1/ Astra就是机器人领域的GPT-3时刻。讽刺的是，如今它终于到来，机器人领域的一些人似乎不愿承认它。也许是因为它（遗憾的是）并非来自一家机器人公司？\n\n2/ 机器人正在成为前沿实验室的又一个垂直领域。在某些方面与编程并无太大不同。为什么要为每个行业重新发明通用智能？\n\n3/ 在此之前，机器人领域太难承保了。没有令人信服的预训练缩放定律，在模型、数据或硬件上没有收敛。难怪一些批评者将其斥为一个碎片化的行业在玩一场昂贵的“演示游戏”。Astra或许终于提供了一条可信的规模化路径。\n\n4/ 机器人基础模型初创公司有其理由。但这理由有多强？论点是：Astra处理系统2（推理），而专用模型保留系统1（技能）和系统0（运动控制）。有道理。但这不已经是一个更窄的价值主张了吗？谁又说边界就止于此？\n\n5/ 跟着人才走。有消息称OpenAI围绕核心Astra模型重组了其30至40人的机器人团队。听说\n@Tesla_Optimus\n也有类似转向通用模型的举动。组织架构图可能比任何演示都能告诉我们更多。\n\n6/ 机器人数据淘金热是真实的。百万小时级的采购项目，有些可能达到数千万小时。有传言称每个前沿实验室的预算接近10亿美元。\n\n7/ 看涨机器人硬件出货量。随着智能变得更易获取，构建有用机器人的壁垒可能会大幅下降。护城河转向可靠性、灵巧性、集成和部署。\n\n8/ 机器人可能推动下一轮半导体和存储超级周期。一个100B参数的模型在边缘运行，仅4位权重就需要约50GB。现在把它乘以数百万台机器人。你以为\n@JensenHuang\n为什么如此痴迷于机器人？\n@elonmusk\n早就预见到了：\nhttps://\nx.com/elonmusk/statu\ns/2114772074438988256?a=ZJpCuCM8Iv8RkRR_g_A&s=20\n…\n\n9/ 自动驾驶能免受通用模型威胁吗？在编程和机器人之后，为什么还假设自动驾驶仍然是专有垂直模型的专属领域？Robotaxi在我看来越来越像一个已解决的问题。但如果且当前沿实验室进军自动驾驶时，我们可能会看到苹果对安卓的动态。想想这对\n$TSLA\n、Waymo和其他OEM意味着什么。\n\n10/ 下一个瓶颈可能不是智能。而是部署。模型的改进速度快于我们在混乱的现实世界中部署机器人的能力。集成、硬件差异、故障恢复和经济学仍然极其艰难。真正的护城河可能是将智能转化为可靠、有利可图的物理工作。\n\n--\n我意识到其中一些观点可能会让人不快，尤其是那些多年来致力于推进机器人硬核工作的人。这不是我的本意。\n\n我分享这些是为了引发辩论，而不是宣布赢家和输家。Astra才推出一月左右，下 definitive 结论还为时过早。更重要的是，当TAM如此巨大——可能是科技界最大的——应该有为不同方法和众多赢家留出的充足空间。\n\n++\n完整尽调报告：\nhttps://\nrobonomics.substack.com/p/robotics-new\n-era-after-astra?r=3hcp4&utm_campaign=post&utm_medium=web\n…"}, {"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "10-26", "l": 8, "r": null, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2116955475652804660", "en": "Thanks \n@Yi__Li\n for the comment! Always appreciate thoughtful pushback, especially from people close to the ground. Would genuinely love to hear your perspective on why you disagree and what you’re seeing that I might be missing. Always eager to learn!", "zh": "1/ Astra是机器人领域的GPT-3时刻。讽刺的是，当它终于到来时，机器人领域的一些人似乎不愿承认。也许是因为它（遗憾地）并非来自一家机器人公司？"}]}, {"id": "n21", "themes": ["公司", "行业"], "date": "2026-10-30", "time": "10-30", "tickers": ["TSLA"], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "10-30", "l": 95, "r": 18, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2116310665459909033", "en": "If \n$TSLA\n robotaxi is at $50m (weekly) runrate ARR (which I think is very possible - math below), then that's probably already at 1/10th \n@Waymo\n 's total gross booking?\n\n> TSLA ARR math (all based on public info):\n\n$TSLA\n disclosed 437k miles/week in Austin. Assuming ~3.5 paid trip miles, at $10-15 per trip. That puts it at over $50M ARR. \nObviously this is a weekly runrate, because TSLA has been scaling v quickly, 10x+ in 3 months. \n\n> Waymo math (all based on public info):\nAssuming 500-600k trips per week or ~4,000 cars on the road (Waymo official commentary), and ~$16 per trip (shorter than Uber trips, but comparable on a per-mile basis), Waymo’s current GMV run-rate is ~$500–600m.\n\nhttps://\nrobonomics.substack.com/p/fact-check-o\nn-self-driving-3q26?r=3hcp4&utm_campaign=post-expanded-share&utm_medium=web\n…", "zh": "如果\n$TSLA\n robotaxi的每周运行率ARR达到5000万美元（我认为这很有可能——计算如下），那么这大概已经达到\n@Waymo\n 总预订毛额的1/10？\n\n> TSLA ARR计算（全部基于公开信息）：\n\n$TSLA\n 披露奥斯汀每周43.7万英里。假设每趟付费行程约3.5英里，每趟10-15美元。这使其ARR超过5000万美元。\n显然这是每周运行率，因为TSLA一直在快速扩张，3个月内增长10倍以上。\n\n> Waymo计算（全部基于公开信息）：\n假设每周500-600k趟行程或路上约4,000辆车（Waymo官方评论），每趟约16美元（比Uber行程短，但按每英里计算相当），Waymo当前的GMV运行率约为5亿至6亿美元。\n\nhttps://\nrobonomics.substack.com/p/fact-check-o\nn-self-driving-3q26?r=3hcp4&utm_campaign=post-expanded-share&utm_medium=web\n…"}]}, {"id": "n35", "themes": ["产业·AI算力"], "date": "2026-11-20", "time": "11-20", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["OrnnExchange"], "tweets": [{"u": "OrnnExchange", "t": "11-20", "l": 55, "r": 4, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2123600228452360484", "en": "Jevons paradox in one chart: tokens get cheaper, demand explodes, compute gets pricier. \n\nWe track both, every day on Ornn Data.", "zh": "杰文斯悖论一张图：代币越来越便宜，需求爆炸式增长，算力越来越贵。"}]}, {"id": "n36", "themes": ["产业·AI算力", "公司"], "date": "2026-11-10", "time": "11-10", "tickers": [], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "11-10", "l": 25, "r": 3, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2120214931731775587", "en": "Congrats to \n@QuanquanGu\n and the Geodesic Intelligence team on the launch of NovaAtom-Lite!\n\nParticularly impressive to see what a small team has been able to accomplish in just a few months. Based on the reported results, NovaAtom-Lite appears to outperform Isomorphic Labs’ IsoDDE and Google DeepMind’s AlphaFold 3 on this specific antibody-antigen structure prediction benchmark.\n\nA great example of how a focused team with strong technical talent can move quickly and push the boundaries. \n\nExcited to see progress on AI drug discovery!", "zh": "祝贺@QuanquanGu和Geodesic Intelligence团队推出NovaAtom-Lite！\n\n尤其令人印象深刻的是，一个小团队在短短几个月内就能取得这样的成果。根据报告的结果，在这个特定的抗体-抗原结构预测基准上，NovaAtom-Lite似乎优于Isomorphic Labs的IsoDDE和Google DeepMind的AlphaFold 3。\n\n这是一个很好的例子，说明一个拥有强大技术人才的专注团队可以快速行动并突破边界。\n\n很高兴看到AI药物发现的进展！"}]}, {"id": "n37", "themes": ["产业·AI算力", "产业·半导体"], "date": "2026-10-26", "time": "10-26", "tickers": ["TSLA"], "accounts": ["FredaDuan"], "tweets": [{"u": "FredaDuan", "t": "10-26", "l": 1100, "r": 237, "url": "https://x.com/i/status/2114772074438988256", "en": "10 Spicy Takes After Talking to 50 Friends at the Frontier of Robotics \n\n1/ Astra IS robotics' GPT-3 moment. Ironically, now that it's finally here, some in robotics seem reluctant to acknowledge it. Perhaps because it (sadly) didn't come from a robotics company?\n\n2/ Robotics is becoming just another vertical for frontier labs. Not so different from coding in some respects. Why reinvent general intelligence for every industry?\n\n3/ Robotics was too hard to underwrite until now. No convincing pretraining scaling law, no convergence on models, data, or hardware. No wonder some critics dismissed it as a fragmented industry playing an expensive \"demo game\". Astra may finally offer a credible path to scale.\n\n4/ Robotics foundation-model startups have a case. But how strong is it? The argument: Astra handles System 2 (reasoning), while specialized models retain System 1 (skills) and System 0 (motor control). Fair. But isn't that already a narrower value proposition? And who says the boundary stops there?\n\n5/ Follow the talent. Word is OpenAI reorganized its 30–40-person robotics team around the core Astra model. Hearing similar moves toward general models at \n@Tesla_Optimus\n. Org charts may tell us more than any demo.\n\n6/ The robotics data gold rush is real. Million-hour procurement programs, some potentially reaching tens of millions of hours. Talk of budgets approaching $1B per frontier lab.\n\n7/ Bullish on robotics hardware volumes. As intelligence becomes more accessible, the barriers to building useful robots could fall dramatically. The moat shifts toward reliability, dexterity, integration, and deployment.\n\n8/ Robotics could fuel the next semiconductor and memory supercycle. A 100B-parameter model running on the edge requires ~50GB just for 4-bit weights. Now multiply that by millions of robots. Why do you think \n@JensenHuang\n is so obsessed with robotics? \n@elonmusk\n saw it coming: \nhttps://\nx.com/elonmusk/statu\ns/2114772074438988256?a=ZJpCuCM8Iv8RkRR_g_A&s=20\n…\n\n9/ Is self-driving immune to the general-model threat? After coding and robotics, why assume self-driving remains the exclusive domain of proprietary, vertical models? Robotaxi increasingly feels like a solved problem to me. But if and when frontier labs move into self-driving, we could see an Apple vs. Android dynamic. Think about the implications for \n$TSLA\n, Waymo, and other OEMs.\n\n10/ The next bottleneck may not be intelligence. It's deployment. Models are improving faster than our ability to deploy robots in the messy real world. Integration, hardware variance, failure recovery, and economics remain brutally hard. The real moat may be turning intelligence into reliable, profitable physical work.\n\n--\nI realize some of these takes may rub people the wrong way, especially those who have spent years doing the hard work of advancing robotics. That's not my intention. \n\nI'm sharing them to spark debate, not to declare winners and losers. Astra has only been out for a month or so, and it's far too early to draw definitive conclusions. More importantly, when the TAM is this enormous - potentially the largest in tech - there should be plenty of room for different approaches and many winners.\n\n++\nFull diligence report: \nhttps://\nrobonomics.substack.com/p/robotics-new\n-era-after-astra?r=3hcp4&utm_campaign=post&utm_medium=web\n…", "zh": "与50位机器人领域前沿的朋友交谈后的10个辛辣观点\n\n1/ Astra就是机器人领域的GPT-3时刻。讽刺的是，如今它终于到来了，机器人领域的一些人似乎不愿承认这一点。也许是因为它（遗憾的是）并非来自一家机器人公司？\n\n2/ 机器人技术正在成为前沿实验室的又一个垂直领域。在某些方面与编程并无太大不同。为什么要为每个行业重新发明通用智能？\n\n3/ 直到现在，机器人技术都太难承保了。没有令人信服的预训练缩放定律，在模型、数据或硬件上都没有收敛。难怪一些批评者将其斥为一个碎片化的行业在玩一场昂贵的“演示游戏”。Astra或许终于提供了一条可信的规模化路径。\n\n4/ 机器人基础模型初创公司有其立足之地。但这立足之地有多强？其论点是：Astra处理系统2（推理），而专用模型保留系统1（技能）和系统0（运动控制）。有道理。但这不已经是一个更狭窄的价值主张了吗？谁又说边界就止于此呢？\n\n5/ 跟着人才走。有消息称OpenAI围绕核心Astra模型重组了其30至40人的机器人团队。听说@Tesla_Optimus也有类似转向通用模型的举动。组织架构图可能比任何演示都更能说明问题。\n\n6/ 机器人数据的淘金热是真实的。百万小时级的采购项目，有些可能达到数千万小时。有传言称每个前沿实验室的预算接近10亿美元。\n\n7/ 看涨机器人硬件出货量。随着智能变得更易获取，构建有用机器人的壁垒可能会大幅下降。护城河转向可靠性、灵巧性、集成和部署。\n\n8/ 机器人技术可能推动下一轮半导体和存储超级周期。一个100B参数的模型在边缘运行，仅4位权重就需要约50GB。现在把它乘以数百万台机器人。你以为@JensenHuang为什么如此痴迷于机器人技术？@elonmusk早就预见到了：\nhttps://\nx.com/elonmusk/statu\ns/2114772074438988256?a=ZJpCuCM8Iv8RkRR_g_A&s=20\n…\n\n9/ 自动驾驶能免受通用模型的威胁吗？在编程和机器人之后，为什么还要假设自动驾驶仍然是专有垂直模型的专属领域？Robotaxi在我看来越来越像一个已被解决的问题。但如果且当前沿实验室进军自动驾驶时，我们可能会看到苹果对安卓的动态。想想这对$TSLA、Waymo和其他OEM意味着什么。\n\n10/ 下一个瓶颈可能不是智能。而是部署。模型的改进速度快于我们在混乱的现实世界中部署机器人的能力。集成、硬件差异、故障恢复和经济效益仍然极其艰难。真正的护城河可能是将智能转化为可靠、有利可图的物理工作。\n\n--\n我意识到其中一些观点可能会让人不快，尤其是那些多年来一直在做推进机器人技术艰苦工作的人。这不是我的本意。\n\n我分享这些是为了引发辩论，而不是宣布赢家和输家。Astra才推出一月左右，现在下 definitive 结论还为时过早。更重要的是，当TAM如此巨大——可能是科技领域最大的——应该有充足的空间容纳不同的方法和众多赢家。\n\n++\n完整尽职调查报告：\nhttps://\nrobonomics.substack.com/p/robotics-new\n-era-after-astra?r=3hcp4&utm_campaign=post&utm_medium=web\n…"}]}];
